{"id": "ba6cefa2-104a-4a46-a5c9-a1484b1db84b", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T17:35:50.342939", "source": "user", "parent_id": "1aba75c8-95c1-4d72-bc93-62a969cd6991", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Thanks. Before we commit to a design, please do only inspection and planning — no results yet.\\n\\n1) Inspect the working environment/repository at /workspace and report what is actually available: any QuaRot implementation, GPTQ/RTN quantizer code, Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct weights or config access, perplexity evaluation scripts (e.g. WikiText-2), and zero-shot harnesses (e.g. lm-evaluation-harness or equivalent). Note explicitly what is absent, since we are offline (network disabled) and have no GPU.\\n\\n2) Report concrete inventory: relevant file/directory names, entry points/config files for quantization, and whether the existing QuaRot code path is LLaMA-specific (hardcoded attention/RMSNorm/RoPE assumptions, head_dim, MLP shape, num_key_value_heads/GQA handling, embedding/vocab sizes) or model-agnostic. Phi-3-mini differs meaningfully from LLaMA-2/3 (e.g. GQA ratio, vocab size ~32k, 32 layers/32 heads with head_dim 96, MLP intermediate size, longer-context RoPE scaling), so I want to know whether the rotation/hadamard placement logic needs adaptation, especially the final head-dim handling that breaks clean Hadamard factorization.\\n\\n3) Propose a design-only experiment plan outline (not the full design): how you would structure the 2x3 factorial — {QuaRot-RTN, QuaRot-GPTQ} x {INT4, INT6, INT8} — against what baselines and controls, what perplexity corpus and zero-shot task battery, what seeds/repeats, and how you would isolate the effect of the rotation from the effect of the rounding algorithm. Include a rough feasibility/resource statement given CPU-only, 2 cores effectively usable, no dataset or model downloads.\\n\\n4) List the consequential assumptions and open choices you are making (e.g. WikiText-2 as the perplexity set, which zero-shot suites, whether non-rotated RTN/GPTQ baselines are in scope, whether FP16 reference is available) and where the source brief is silent.\\n\\nKeep this to inspection findings + proposed approach + assumptions. I will review and we can then proceed.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How well does QuaRot generalize to non-LLAMA models like Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct? Specifically, how do RTN and GPTQ compare in perplexity and zero-shot accuracy across 4-bit, 6-bit, and 8-bit quantization?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_1\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_3\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_4\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_6\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_8\", \"neurips2024/94328/9:setup_11\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
