te_up_proj` bias=False, `down_proj` bias=False. Yes — Phi3 dense uses no bias (the original Phi-3 had bias in some layers? microsoft/phi-3 papers mention no biases in the released transformers implementation). Actually there is `qkv_proj` with bias... I'm not 100% sure. In HF modeling_phi3.py, `QKVProj` etc. are all `bias=False` (they removed biases; Phi3 has \"no biases\" comment). I recall a comment in modeling_phi3.py: \"Phi3ForCausalLM ... biases removed\". Hmm, the original Phi-3 release: \"Phi-3-mini ... we removed all biases\" — I believe Phi-3 mini has no biases. But there is a special detail: in HF, `embed_tokens` and `lm_head` are tied? Phi-3: tie_word_embeddings: true for phi-3-mini? Actually Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct has `tie_word_embeddings: true` (Phi models tie embeddings with LM head). Hmm, Phi-3-mini 3.8B: vocab 32064 × 3072 = 98.5M params for embedding; total params 3.8B. Phi-3 paper says \"we do not tie embeddings\". I recall the config `\"tie_word_embeddings\": false` for Phi-3? For phi-3-mini-4k-instruct the model.safetensors index contains lm_head.weight? I think Phi-3 does NOT tie (they trained untied). Hmm. I should flag this as \"must verify from config.json\" rather than assert. Good — I'll flag as verification item.\n\nAlso Phi-3 uses `logit_scale` = 1.0 (Phi3Config has logit_scale field, used in some Phi versions), `emb_layernorm`? No, that's for phi-1.5 with parallel attn. Phi-3-mini is standard sequential attention+MLP with fused qkv_proj/gate_up_proj, RMSNorm, LongRoPE (long_factor/short_factor with mscale and rope_type \"longrope\"), plus `resblock_post_backward` in phi-3-medium.\n\nKey adaptations needed for Phi-3:\n1. Rotation search space / `--rotation_mode` and merged RMSNorm folding: Phi-3's qkv_proj is fused → the rotation must be applied to the whole fused qkv_proj output? Actually QuaRot rotates the hidden dim of inputs, and for the attention output of q/k it applies per-head online Hadamard (H_admm offline rotation of v/o_proj).