e with answer, evidence, assumptions, uncertainties. The answer should include the outline of approach (not the full design), consequential choices, uncertainties. But the researcher asked 4 questions; I should answer all in the answer, since private tool output isn't automatically shared. Keep it organized but reasonably compact.\n\nLength: substantial but organized. Let's write.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "## 1) Environment inventory — what is actually here (verified)\n\n**Present:** essentially nothing but a task stub.\n- `/workspace` contains exactly one file: `task.json` (499 B). No git repo, no code, no hidden files (`ls -laR` shows only `.`/`..`/`task.json`).\n- Toolchain binaries exist: `gcc/g++-15`, `make`, `git`, `git-lfs`, `curl`, `wget`. No `cmake`, no `nvcc`.\n- Interpreter: Python **3.14.4**, 105 packages — all distro/system tooling (ansible, apt, dbus, PIL, Jinja, certifi…).\n\n**Absent (each verified by direct probe):**\n- **No QuaRot implementation** anywhere on the mounted FS (`find / -xdev -iname '*quarot*'` → empty).\n- **No GPTQ/RTN/quantizer code** (`*gptq*` → empty), no `lm-evaluation-harness`/`lm_eval`, no perplexity script, no GPT-FAQ/SparseGPT/OmniQuant lineage code.\n- **No model weights or config**: no `*.safetensors`, `*.gguf`, or model `*.bin`; no `*phi-3*`/`*phi3*` paths; `~/.cache` does not exist; `/home/actor` empty; `datasets: []` in task.json.\n- **No ML stack at all**: `import torch` → ModuleNotFoundError, `import numpy` → ModuleNotFoundError; pip list has no torch/transformers/accelerate/datasets/safetensors/tokenizers/scipy/numpy.\n- **Offline**: DNS fails (`gaierror` on pypi.org:443); `pip install numpy` fails outright; no wheelhouse (`find / -xdev -name '*.whl'` → empty). Compilers are therefore useless — there is nothing to build from and no way to fetch source.\n- Python **3.14** is itself a risk: QuaRot pins torch 2.2–2.3 / transformers ~4.40–4.43, which have no cp314 wheels. Even with network, a conda py3.10/3.11 env would be mandatory.\n\n**Resources (measured, with one discrepancy vs the brief):** `nproc=224`, `sched_getaffinity=224` (list `0-223`), no visible cgroup `cpu.max`. So the \"2 cores effectively usable\" claim is **not confirmable from inside** the sandbox — I treat it as a scheduler/policy constraint, not an observed one. RAM is ample: 2011 GB total, ~1935 GB available. **Disk is the real squeeze:** `/workspace` is an NFS mount at 100% with only **~6–7 GB free**; `/tmp` is tmpfs with ~1 TB. Phi-3-mini BF16 weights (~7.9 GB) will *not* fit on `/workspace` → all scratch must live in `/tmp`, `/workspace` for metrics only.\n\n**Conclusion:** this environment supports *design only*. Nothing about Phi-3, QuaRot, or perplexity can be executed or even smoke-tested here (no numpy). Every execution statement below is a plan for a different host (GPU + network + pre-fetched artifacts), and no experiment has been run.\n\n## 2) Is the QuaRot code path LLaMA-specific? — Yes, substantially\n\nImportant caveat: **the repo is absent here**, so everything in this section is model-knowledge of upstream `astone3207/QuaRot` (NeurIPS 2024 release), **not inspection**. It must be re-verified against the actual tree before implementation.\n\nArchitecture of that codebase (GPT-FAQ/SparseGPT lineage): `main.py` (argparse: `--model`, `--model_args`, `--rotation_mode {full,none,partial,residual}`, `--quant_method {normal,gptq}`, `--w_bits/--a_bits/--k_bits/--v_bits`, `--quant_dataset`, `--nsamples`, `--tasks`, `--sessions`) → `utils/quarot_utils.py` (`rotate_model`, `merge_ln`/`fuse_ln_weight_into_proj`, rotation-matrix cache, `find_layers` with hardcoded key dicts) → `utils/hadamard_matrix.py` (`get_had` fast Walsh–Hadamard, **asserts power-of-two size**) → `utils/gptq_utils/*` (parallel GPTQ, per-module Hessian, quantizer) → `utils/data_utils.py` (C4/ptb/Open-LLAMA calibration) → **per-model hand-copied modeling files** `models/llama.py`, `models/llama_gptq.py`, `models/opt.py`, `models/mpt.py`, with the rotation/quant hooks inserted inline into `LlamaAttention`/`LlamaMLP`, and module selection via hardcoded name lists (`llama_attention_keys`, `llama_mlp_keys`, …). So it is **model-specific by construction**, and a Phi-3 port means writing `models/phi3.py` + `phi3_*` key sets, not flipping a flag.\n\nPhi-3-mini deltas that break the LLaMA assumptions (config values from memory of `microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct/config.json` — **must be verified**): hidden 3072, intermediate 8192, 32 layers, 32 heads, **head_dim = 96 (no explicit field)**, `num_key_value_heads = 32`, vocab 32064 (padded), eos 32000/`<|end|>`, `rope_scaling: longrope` with short/long_factor + mscale, `use_mlp_bias: false`, fused `qkv_proj` and `gate_up_proj`.\n\nConcrete adaptation items, ranked by severity:\n1. **head_dim 96 breaks the Hadamard factorization — the central issue.** QuaRot's online Hadamards are applied per head to *post-RoPE* q and k (so HᵀH cancels exactly in the score, no RoPE-commutation constraint), plus per-head offline rotations for v/o_proj. All of these need a 96×96 Hadamard; the fast Walsh–Hadamard path is powers-of-two only and the repo asserts that. Options: (a) **block-diagonal H₃₂⊕H₃₂⊕H₃₂** (3|96) — exactly orthogonal, keeps fast transform, weaker mixing than a full 96 Hadamard; (b) a dense known-existing **Had(96)** (existence known, 96=4·24; not Sylvester/Paley-direct, so it must be sourced or constructed) as a shipped ±1 file — dense matmul is cheap on CPU; (c) seeded random orthogonal 96×96 — use as the *control arm*, not as \"QuaRot\".\n2. **hidden=3072 is also not a power of two** (3·1024) — the residual-stream offline rotation G has the same problem, which upstream never hits because LLaMA-2/3 hidden sizes are 4096. Natural analogue: block-diag(H₁₀₂₄)×3. Note intermediate 8192 = 2¹³ is clean, so the MLP-side online Hadamard (their Thm 3.2) is unaffected.\n3. **Fused projections.** LLaMA-shaped code rotates `q_proj/k_proj/v_proj` and `gate_proj/up_proj` separately; Phi-3 has one `qkv_proj` (3·3072) and one `gate_up_proj` (2·8192). Need head-aligned slicing of the fused weight (or un-fuse into views). Harmless for GPTQ (per-module Hessians, groups along the input dim), fatal for rotation folding if done naively.\n4. **LongRoPE + `trust_remote_code` vs native `transformers.models.phi3`.** LongRoPE does not interact with the quantization math, but the RoPE code path must be byte-identical between the FP16 reference and every quantized cell, or the comparison is confounded by a modeling diff. Pin one modeling path for all cells. Verify `attention_scaling`/softcap fields.\n5. **Possible tied embeddings.** If `tie_word_embeddings` is true, folding G into `embed_tokens` invalidates the tie for `lm_head` (upstream assumes untied). Keep `lm_head`/embeddings unquantized and resolve the tie explicitly.\n6. **GQA premise in your brief does not appear to hold.** Phi-3-mini has `num_key_value_heads = 32` → **GQA ratio 1 (plain MHA)**. The `repeat_kv` path is exercised trivially, so this experiment will *not* stress GQA. If GQA handling is something you want tested, Phi-3-small-128k (GQA + MoE) or LLaMA-3-8B (28/8, ratio 3.5) is the right vehicle. Worth correcting before we build.\n7. `RMSNorm` merging, `head_dim` inference from `hidden//heads`, vocab 32064/padded rows, chat-template handling in the harness, and outlier statistics that differ from LLaMA (Phi-3 attention-sink/massive-activation pattern is not the same) all need porting checks.\n\n## 3) Proposed design outline (outline only — full design after your sign-off)\n\n**Corrected factorial.** Your 2×3 ({QuaRot-RTN, QuaRot-GPTQ}×{4,6,8}) cannot answer \"how well does QuaRot generalize\" or \"rotation vs rounding\", because rotation is not crossed with anything. Propose **2×2×3 = 12 cells**: R {Identity, QuaRot-Hadamard} × A {RTN, GPTQ} × B {4, 6, 8}, plus (i) BF16 reference, (ii) R=QuaRot @ 16-bit no-quant **exactness gate**, and (iii) an optional 3rd rotation level R′ = **random orthogonal, same placement** (3 cells). Weight-only (a/k/v in FP16) for all cells; groupsize fixed per algorithm with a 4-bit sensitivity check {g=128, g=-1}.\n\n**Why the R′ arm matters specifically here:** because Had(96)/Had(3072) must be *approximated* by block-diagonal Hadamard on Phi-3, any residual Phi-3-vs-LLaMA gap could come from (a) rotation placement/exactness, (b) Hadamard structure/weak mixing at dim 96, or (c) genuinely different Phi-3 outlier geometry. R vs R′ within the same placement separates (a)+(c) from (b). Without it the mechanism claim is unidentifiable.\n\n**Controls, each buying a specific inference:**\n- BF16 reference → Δppl/Δacc anchor and \"0-bit\" point.\n- Identity-rotation RTN and GPTQ → the rotation effect estimated *within* each algorithm×bit; also the only way to see whether RTN-vs-GPTQ ranking flips (expected: rotation compresses the gap at 4 bits, since Hessian-guided rounding and outlier isotropization are partially redundant).\n- QuaRot @ 16-bit → hard gate: must match BF16 ppl within numerical noise. If it doesn't, the port is broken and no cell is interpretable. Run this before the grid.\n- Same calibration set/size, same dtype, same excluded modules (embed/lm_head), same sym/asym choice for both algorithms → prevents RTN being advantaged by more calibration tokens or by per-channel asymmetry.\n- Optional LLaMA-3-8B (or Llama-2-7B) 4-bit QuaRot-RTN/GPTQ positive control to show our pipeline reproduces published QuaRot numbers, making Phi-3 a real generalization test rather than a port-bug artifact.\n- Mechanism diagnostics (cheap, CPU-friendly, high value): per-channel activation max/median ratio, kurtosis and top-1% energy fraction before vs after rotation; per-layer quantization error ‖ŴX−WX‖_F; GPTQ Hessian condition number and `percdamp` sensitivity.\n\n**Perplexity:** WikiText-2 test, 4096-token non-overlapping windows, no stride (plus a 2048 slice for comparability with published QuaRot tables). Secondary PTB only if budget allows. Report Δppl and % degradation, never raw ppl alone.\n\n**Zero-shot:** lm-evaluation-harness (v0.4.x), core battery piqa, arc_easy, arc_challenge, hellaswag, winogrande, openbookqa (0-shot, loglikelihood) + mmlu (5-shot) + truthfulqa_mc + gsm8k (8-shot CoT) as the deliberately brittle stress tasks. Log-likelihood tasks are deterministic given a cell; state that binomial SEs are large (winogrande n=1267 → ≈1.4 pp) and use **paired McNemar tests on the same examples**, never independent-proportion comparisons on subsamples.\n\n**Seeds/repeats:** quantization itself is deterministic; randomness enters via calibration subset and random-rotation draws. Fix 3 disjoint calibration subsets (128×4096 C4) and 3 random-rotation seeds, and run the 3 repeats on the **4-bit cells** (where variance and the ranking question live); 1–2 repeats at 6/8 bits with the expectation of ceiling-saturation.\n\n**Analysis:** Δppl and Δacc per cell; two-way rotation×algorithm interaction contrast at 4 and 6 bits, interaction as the pre-registered headline; rotation effect paired by (calibration subset, seed); report all cells including failures.\n\n**Feasibility (CPU-only, 2 usable cores, no downloads).** *In this container: nothing runs.* On a CPU-only execution host: Phi-3-mini ≈3.8B params, ~7.6 GB BF16 weights — RAM fine, throughput not. ~2·P ≈ 7.6 GFLOP/token; realistic 2-core bf16 prefill ~10–50 tok/s → WikiText-2 test (~400k tok) ≈ 2–6 h per cell; GPTQ calibration adds ~2–8 h per cell (forward passes dominate; the ≤8192² Cholesky solves are seconds). RTN itself is minutes. The zero-shot battery is the killer: the 6 core tasks (~72k prompts) are tens of core-hours per cell → **12 cells × full battery is not feasible at 2 cores**. Proposed tiering: **T0** exactness gate (~1 h); **T1** all 12 cells on WikiText-2 ppl + fixed-seed 25% subsamples of each zero-shot task (paired within cell); **T2** full battery for 4-bit cells + BF16 + Identity-4bit only; **T3** LLaMA control, groupsize/damp sensitivity, R′ arm. Disk: `/tmp` tmpfs for weights/Hessians; `/workspace` (6 GB free) for metric JSON only.\n\n## 4) Consequential assumptions / where the brief is silent\n\nAssumptions (mine, not task-given): (1) Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct BF16 weights obtainable on some other host; (2) my config numbers above are from memory and must be read off `config.json` — in particular the GQA premise; (3) upstream QuaRot is the intended codebase and my LLaMA-specificity claims are unverified model knowledge, to be re-derived if a fork is used; (4) **weight-only** W4/W6/W8 with FP16 activations and KV cache (the brief is silent, and RTN-vs-GPTQ is a weight-rounding contrast — W4A4 would be a different experiment); (5) WikiText-2 as primary ppl set; (6) lm-eval-harness with the listed battery and my shot counts; (7) non-rotated RTN/GPTQ baselines treated as **required**, not optional; (8) BF16/FP16 reference obtainable; (9) calibration on C4 128×4096 identical across all cells, notwithstanding the base-style-C4-vs-instruct-model mismatch; (10) chat-template formatting fixed across cells.\n\nOpen choices needing your decision: (a) scope — accept the 2×2×3 (+R′) expansion vs the literal 2×3; (b) which Hadamard-for-96 route (block-diag H₃₂ vs dense Had(96)); (c) is a LLaMA positive control in scope (it is what makes \"generalizes\" measurable); (d) full battery vs T1/T2 tiering; (e) an explicit quantitative success criterion for \"generalizes well\" (the brief does not define one — I propose: relative ppl degradation at matched bits vs the LLaMA control, plus persistence of the rotation×algorithm interaction sign); (f) whether W4A16 vs W4A4 matters to you. I'd also like to confirm the 2-core constraint, since the box reports 224.", "evidence": "All environment claims are from executed probes in this session; code-architecture claims are model knowledge of upstream QuaRot, explicitly not inspected (repo absent).\n\nVERIFIED BY EXECUTION:\n- `ls -laR /workspace` → only `task.json` (499 B); `git status` → \"not a git repository\". task.json contents: question text + \"documents\": {\"track.md\": \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"}, datasets: [], gpu_enabled: false.\n- `find / -xdev -iname '*quarot*' -o -iname '*gptq*' -o -iname '*phi-3*' -o -iname '*phi3*'` → empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.safetensors' -o -name '*.gguf' -o -name '*.bin' -path '*model*'` → empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.whl'` → empty.\n- `pip list` = 105 packages, all distro tooling; grep for torch|transformers|datasets|accelerate|hugging|numpy|scipy|safetensors|tokenizers|eval|ptq|sklearn → no matches. `import torch` and `import numpy` → ModuleNotFoundError.\n- Network: socket.create_connection(('pypi.org',443)) → gaierror \"[Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution\"; `pip install numpy` → fails (FileNotFoundError inside pip); no /etc/pip.conf. `ls -la ~/.cache` → No such file; /home/actor empty. /tmp empty.\n- Directories /opt /srv /data /models /mnt /media /shared /research: none exist. /usr/local/share has only ca-certificates, fonts, man, sgml, xml.\n- `nproc`=224; `os.sched_getaffinity(0)`=224; `taskset -pc` → \"0-223\"; no /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max. CPU: Intel Xeon Platinum 8570. `free -g`: 2011 GB total, 1935 available, 0 swap.\n- `df`: /workspace = 1.0T, 1018G used, 6.2G avail, 100%; /tmp tmpfs 1006G free. 100 MB write probe to /workspace succeeded (space is tight but writable).\n- /usr/bin contains gcc, gcc-15, g++, g++-15, cc, make, git, git-lfs, curl, wget; no cmake, no nvcc.\n\nUNVERIFIED / REPO-KNOWLEDGE-BASED (flagged as such in the answer): upstream QuaRot layout (main.py flags, models/llama.py + llama_gptq.py copies, utils/quarot_utils.py rotate_model/merge_ln/find_layers key dicts, utils/hadamard_matrix.py power-of-two assertion, utils/gptq_utils, C4/ptb calibration); Phi-3-mini config values (hidden 3072, intermediate 8192, 32 layers/32 heads, head_dim 96, num_key_value_heads 32, vocab 32064, longrope, use_mlp_bias false, fused qkv_proj/gate_up_proj, possible tied embeddings).", "assumptions": ["No experiment has been run; this is design only. The task itself states 'repositories and compute are not required', and the container has no ML stack, no weights, no datasets and no network, so nothing here is executable.", "Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct weights and config would be obtainable on a different (non-sandbox) execution host with network/GPU.", "The intended codebase is upstream astone3207/QuaRot (NeurIPS 2024 release); all LLaMA-specificity findings are model knowledge about that repo, not inspection, since the repo is absent from /workspace.", "Phi-3-mini config values cited (head_dim 96, num_key_value_heads=32, hidden 3072, intermediate 8192, vocab 32064, longrope, fused qkv/gate_up, possible tied embeddings) are from memory of the release config and must be verified against config.json before implementation.", "Weight-only quantization is intended: W4/W6/W8 with FP16 activations and FP16 KV cache. The brief does not state this; W4A4 would be a different experiment.", "WikiText-2 test split is the perplexity corpus (brief is silent; QuaRot also reports PTB/C4).", "lm-evaluation-harness (v0.4.x) is the zero-shot harness, with the task battery and shot counts I proposed; the brief does not name any suite.", "Non-rotated RTN and non-rotated GPTQ baselines are in scope and are required, not optional - without crossing rotation with algorithm the 2x3 cannot answer the question.", "An FP16/BF16 Phi-3 reference run is available and is used both as the degradation anchor and as the exactness gate for the rotation port.", "Calibration uses C4, 128 samples x 4096 tokens, identical across all cells; the base-C4 vs instruct-model text-style mismatch is accepted but held constant.", "The '2 cores effectively usable' limit is a scheduler policy, not something observable in this container (which reports 224 CPUs); throughput estimates are conditioned on it.", "The brief's premise that Phi-3-mini differs from LLaMA via GQA ratio appears incorrect (kv_heads=32 => plain MHA); head_dim=96 and non-power-of-two hidden=3072 are the real Hadamard-breaking deltas."], "uncertainties": ["Whether the target QuaRot code is upstream or an internal fork - the adaptation checklist (models/phi3.py port, find_layers key sets, fused-projection handling) must be re-derived from the actual tree once available.", "Which Hadamard-for-head_dim-96 route to take: block-diagonal H32x3 (fast, weaker mixing) vs a dense shipped Had(96) (stronger mixing, needs a verified construction/source). This is a consequential choice for the headline claim.", "Whether the 'generalizes well' criterion should be defined at all, and if so against what reference (proposed: matched-bit relative ppl degradation vs a LLaMA-3-8B control plus persistence of the rotation x algorithm interaction sign). The brief defines nothing.", "Whether a LLaMA positive control is in budget - without it, 'generalization' has no baseline and port bugs cannot be distinguished from a genuine Phi-3 finding.", "Whether the full zero-shot battery is affordable on CPU; my tiering (25% paired subsamples for all cells, full battery only at 4-bit + reference) is a budget-driven compromise that halves per-task power and must be analyzed with McNemar paired tests.", "Disk: /workspace has only ~6 GB free, so any real run needs /tmp tmpfs or a larger volume; unverified whether that holds on the execution host.", "Tied embeddings on Phi-3-mini (unverified) would change how the residual-stream rotation is folded and whether lm_head can stay in FP16 cleanly.", "Whether Phi-3's attention scaling / longrope mscale settings in a given transformers version alter the FP16 reference ppl, which would silently confound all deltas unless one modeling path is pinned.", "The effective core count on the real execution host, and hence whether the CPU-only tiering above is even sufficient."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bb757d25578ba413", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-bb757d25578ba413", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"## 1) Environment inventory \\u2014 what is actually here (verified)\\n\\n**Present:** essentially nothing but a task stub.\\n- `/workspace` contains exactly one file: `task.json` (499 B). No git repo, no code, no hidden files (`ls -laR` shows only `.`/`..`/`task.json`).\\n- Toolchain binaries exist: `gcc/g++-15`, `make`, `git`, `git-lfs`, `curl`, `wget`. No `cmake`, no `nvcc`.\\n- Interpreter: Python **3.14.4**, 105 packages \\u2014 all distro/system tooling (ansible, apt, dbus, PIL, Jinja, certifi\\u2026).\\n\\n**Absent (each verified by direct probe):**\\n- **No QuaRot implementation** anywhere on the mounted FS (`find / -xdev -iname '*quarot*'` \\u2192 empty).\\n- **No GPTQ/RTN/quantizer code** (`*gptq*` \\u2192 empty), no `lm-evaluation-harness`/`lm_eval`, no perplexity script, no GPT-FAQ/SparseGPT/OmniQuant lineage code.\\n- **No model weights or config**: no `*.safetensors`, `*.gguf`, or model `*.bin`; no `*phi-3*`/`*phi3*` paths; `~/.cache` does not exist; `/home/actor` empty; `datasets: []` in task.json.\\n- **No ML stack at all**: `import torch` \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError, `import numpy` \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError; pip list has no torch/transformers/accelerate/datasets/safetensors/tokenizers/scipy/numpy.\\n- **Offline**: DNS fails (`gaierror` on pypi.org:443); `pip install numpy` fails outright; no wheelhouse (`find / -xdev -name '*.whl'` \\u2192 empty). Compilers are therefore useless \\u2014 there is nothing to build from and no way to fetch source.\\n- Python **3.14** is itself a risk: QuaRot pins torch 2.2\\u20132.3 / transformers ~4.40\\u20134.43, which have no cp314 wheels. Even with network, a conda py3.10/3.11 env would be mandatory.\\n\\n**Resources (measured, with one discrepancy vs the brief):** `nproc=224`, `sched_getaffinity=224` (list `0-223`), no visible cgroup `cpu.max`. So the \\\"2 cores effectively usable\\\" claim is **not confirmable from inside** the sandbox \\u2014 I treat it as a scheduler/policy constraint, not an observed one. RAM is ample: 2011 GB total, ~1935 GB available. **Disk is the real squeeze:** `/workspace` is an NFS mount at 100% with only **~6\\u20137 GB free**; `/tmp` is tmpfs with ~1 TB. Phi-3-mini BF16 weights (~7.9 GB) will *not* fit on `/workspace` \\u2192 all scratch must live in `/tmp`, `/workspace` for metrics only.\\n\\n**Conclusion:** this environment supports *design only*. Nothing about Phi-3, QuaRot, or perplexity can be executed or even smoke-tested here (no numpy). Every execution statement below is a plan for a different host (GPU + network + pre-fetched artifacts), and no experiment has been run.\\n\\n## 2) Is the QuaRot code path LLaMA-specific? \\u2014 Yes, substantially\\n\\nImportant caveat: **the repo is absent here**, so everything in this section is model-knowledge of upstream `astone3207/QuaRot` (NeurIPS 2024 release), **not inspection**. It must be re-verified against the actual tree before implementation.\\n\\nArchitecture of that codebase (GPT-FAQ/SparseGPT lineage): `main.py` (argparse: `--model`, `--model_args`, `--rotation_mode {full,none,partial,residual}`, `--quant_method {normal,gptq}`, `--w_bits/--a_bits/--k_bits/--v_bits`, `--quant_dataset`, `--nsamples`, `--tasks`, `--sessions`) \\u2192 `utils/quarot_utils.py` (`rotate_model`, `merge_ln`/`fuse_ln_weight_into_proj`, rotation-matrix cache, `find_layers` with hardcoded key dicts) \\u2192 `utils/hadamard_matrix.py` (`get_had` fast Walsh\\u2013Hadamard, **asserts power-of-two size**) \\u2192 `utils/gptq_utils/*` (parallel GPTQ, per-module Hessian, quantizer) \\u2192 `utils/data_utils.py` (C4/ptb/Open-LLAMA calibration) \\u2192 **per-model hand-copied modeling files** `models/llama.py`, `models/llama_gptq.py`, `models/opt.py`, `models/mpt.py`, with the rotation/quant hooks inserted inline into `LlamaAttention`/`LlamaMLP`, and module selection via hardcoded name lists (`llama_attention_keys`, `llama_mlp_keys`, \\u2026). So it is **model-specific by construction**, and a Phi-3 port means writing `models/phi3.py` + `phi3_*` key sets, not flipping a flag.\\n\\nPhi-3-mini deltas that break the LLaMA assumptions (config values from memory of `microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct/config.json` \\u2014 **must be verified**): hidden 3072, intermediate 8192, 32 layers, 32 heads, **head_dim = 96 (no explicit field)**, `num_key_value_heads = 32`, vocab 32064 (padded), eos 32000/`<|end|>`, `rope_scaling: longrope` with short/long_factor + mscale, `use_mlp_bias: false`, fused `qkv_proj` and `gate_up_proj`.\\n\\nConcrete adaptation items, ranked by severity:\\n1. **head_dim 96 breaks the Hadamard factorization \\u2014 the central issue.** QuaRot's online Hadamards are applied per head to *post-RoPE* q and k (so H\\u1d40H cancels exactly in the score, no RoPE-commutation constraint), plus per-head offline rotations for v/o_proj. All of these need a 96\\u00d796 Hadamard; the fast Walsh\\u2013Hadamard path is powers-of-two only and the repo asserts that. Options: (a) **block-diagonal H\\u2083\\u2082\\u2295H\\u2083\\u2082\\u2295H\\u2083\\u2082** (3|96) \\u2014 exactly orthogonal, keeps fast transform, weaker mixing than a full 96 Hadamard; (b) a dense known-existing **Had(96)** (existence known, 96=4\\u00b724; not Sylvester/Paley-direct, so it must be sourced or constructed) as a shipped \\u00b11 file \\u2014 dense matmul is cheap on CPU; (c) seeded random orthogonal 96\\u00d796 \\u2014 use as the *control arm*, not as \\\"QuaRot\\\".\\n2. **hidden=3072 is also not a power of two** (3\\u00b71024) \\u2014 the residual-stream offline rotation G has the same problem, which upstream never hits because LLaMA-2/3 hidden sizes are 4096. Natural analogue: block-diag(H\\u2081\\u2080\\u2082\\u2084)\\u00d73. Note intermediate 8192 = 2\\u00b9\\u00b3 is clean, so the MLP-side online Hadamard (their Thm 3.2) is unaffected.\\n3. **Fused projections.** LLaMA-shaped code rotates `q_proj/k_proj/v_proj` and `gate_proj/up_proj` separately; Phi-3 has one `qkv_proj` (3\\u00b73072) and one `gate_up_proj` (2\\u00b78192). Need head-aligned slicing of the fused weight (or un-fuse into views). Harmless for GPTQ (per-module Hessians, groups along the input dim), fatal for rotation folding if done naively.\\n4. **LongRoPE + `trust_remote_code` vs native `transformers.models.phi3`.** LongRoPE does not interact with the quantization math, but the RoPE code path must be byte-identical between the FP16 reference and every quantized cell, or the comparison is confounded by a modeling diff. Pin one modeling path for all cells. Verify `attention_scaling`/softcap fields.\\n5. **Possible tied embeddings.** If `tie_word_embeddings` is true, folding G into `embed_tokens` invalidates the tie for `lm_head` (upstream assumes untied). Keep `lm_head`/embeddings unquantized and resolve the tie explicitly.\\n6. **GQA premise in your brief does not appear to hold.** Phi-3-mini has `num_key_value_heads = 32` \\u2192 **GQA ratio 1 (plain MHA)**. The `repeat_kv` path is exercised trivially, so this experiment will *not* stress GQA. If GQA handling is something you want tested, Phi-3-small-128k (GQA + MoE) or LLaMA-3-8B (28/8, ratio 3.5) is the right vehicle. Worth correcting before we build.\\n7. `RMSNorm` merging, `head_dim` inference from `hidden//heads`, vocab 32064/padded rows, chat-template handling in the harness, and outlier statistics that differ from LLaMA (Phi-3 attention-sink/massive-activation pattern is not the same) all need porting checks.\\n\\n## 3) Proposed design outline (outline only \\u2014 full design after your sign-off)\\n\\n**Corrected factorial.** Your 2\\u00d73 ({QuaRot-RTN, QuaRot-GPTQ}\\u00d7{4,6,8}) cannot answer \\\"how well does QuaRot generalize\\\" or \\\"rotation vs rounding\\\", because rotation is not crossed with anything. Propose **2\\u00d72\\u00d73 = 12 cells**: R {Identity, QuaRot-Hadamard} \\u00d7 A {RTN, GPTQ} \\u00d7 B {4, 6, 8}, plus (i) BF16 reference, (ii) R=QuaRot @ 16-bit no-quant **exactness gate**, and (iii) an optional 3rd rotation level R\\u2032 = **random orthogonal, same placement** (3 cells). Weight-only (a/k/v in FP16) for all cells; groupsize fixed per algorithm with a 4-bit sensitivity check {g=128, g=-1}.\\n\\n**Why the R\\u2032 arm matters specifically here:** because Had(96)/Had(3072) must be *approximated* by block-diagonal Hadamard on Phi-3, any residual Phi-3-vs-LLaMA gap could come from (a) rotation placement/exactness, (b) Hadamard structure/weak mixing at dim 96, or (c) genuinely different Phi-3 outlier geometry. R vs R\\u2032 within the same placement separates (a)+(c) from (b). Without it the mechanism claim is unidentifiable.\\n\\n**Controls, each buying a specific inference:**\\n- BF16 reference \\u2192 \\u0394ppl/\\u0394acc anchor and \\\"0-bit\\\" point.\\n- Identity-rotation RTN and GPTQ \\u2192 the rotation effect estimated *within* each algorithm\\u00d7bit; also the only way to see whether RTN-vs-GPTQ ranking flips (expected: rotation compresses the gap at 4 bits, since Hessian-guided rounding and outlier isotropization are partially redundant).\\n- QuaRot @ 16-bit \\u2192 hard gate: must match BF16 ppl within numerical noise. If it doesn't, the port is broken and no cell is interpretable. Run this before the grid.\\n- Same calibration set/size, same dtype, same excluded modules (embed/lm_head), same sym/asym choice for both algorithms \\u2192 prevents RTN being advantaged by more calibration tokens or by per-channel asymmetry.\\n- Optional LLaMA-3-8B (or Llama-2-7B) 4-bit QuaRot-RTN/GPTQ positive control to show our pipeline reproduces published QuaRot numbers, making Phi-3 a real generalization test rather than a port-bug artifact.\\n- Mechanism diagnostics (cheap, CPU-friendly, high value): per-channel activation max/median ratio, kurtosis and top-1% energy fraction before vs after rotation; per-layer quantization error \\u2016\\u0174X\\u2212WX\\u2016_F; GPTQ Hessian condition number and `percdamp` sensitivity.\\n\\n**Perplexity:** WikiText-2 test, 4096-token non-overlapping windows, no stride (plus a 2048 slice for comparability with published QuaRot tables). Secondary PTB only if budget allows. Report \\u0394ppl and % degradation, never raw ppl alone.\\n\\n**Zero-shot:** lm-evaluation-harness (v0.4.x), core battery piqa, arc_easy, arc_challenge, hellaswag, winogrande, openbookqa (0-shot, loglikelihood) + mmlu (5-shot) + truthfulqa_mc + gsm8k (8-shot CoT) as the deliberately brittle stress tasks. Log-likelihood tasks are deterministic given a cell; state that binomial SEs are large (winogrande n=1267 \\u2192 \\u22481.4 pp) and use **paired McNemar tests on the same examples**, never independent-proportion comparisons on subsamples.\\n\\n**Seeds/repeats:** quantization itself is deterministic; randomness enters via calibration subset and random-rotation draws. Fix 3 disjoint calibration subsets (128\\u00d74096 C4) and 3 random-rotation seeds, and run the 3 repeats on the **4-bit cells** (where variance and the ranking question live); 1\\u20132 repeats at 6/8 bits with the expectation of ceiling-saturation.\\n\\n**Analysis:** \\u0394ppl and \\u0394acc per cell; two-way rotation\\u00d7algorithm interaction contrast at 4 and 6 bits, interaction as the pre-registered headline; rotation effect paired by (calibration subset, seed); report all cells including failures.\\n\\n**Feasibility (CPU-only, 2 usable cores, no downloads).** *In this container: nothing runs.* On a CPU-only execution host: Phi-3-mini \\u22483.8B params, ~7.6 GB BF16 weights \\u2014 RAM fine, throughput not. ~2\\u00b7P \\u2248 7.6 GFLOP/token; realistic 2-core bf16 prefill ~10\\u201350 tok/s \\u2192 WikiText-2 test (~400k tok) \\u2248 2\\u20136 h per cell; GPTQ calibration adds ~2\\u20138 h per cell (forward passes dominate; the \\u22648192\\u00b2 Cholesky solves are seconds). RTN itself is minutes. The zero-shot battery is the killer: the 6 core tasks (~72k prompts) are tens of core-hours per cell \\u2192 **12 cells \\u00d7 full battery is not feasible at 2 cores**. Proposed tiering: **T0** exactness gate (~1 h); **T1** all 12 cells on WikiText-2 ppl + fixed-seed 25% subsamples of each zero-shot task (paired within cell); **T2** full battery for 4-bit cells + BF16 + Identity-4bit only; **T3** LLaMA control, groupsize/damp sensitivity, R\\u2032 arm. Disk: `/tmp` tmpfs for weights/Hessians; `/workspace` (6 GB free) for metric JSON only.\\n\\n## 4) Consequential assumptions / where the brief is silent\\n\\nAssumptions (mine, not task-given): (1) Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct BF16 weights obtainable on some other host; (2) my config numbers above are from memory and must be read off `config.json` \\u2014 in particular the GQA premise; (3) upstream QuaRot is the intended codebase and my LLaMA-specificity claims are unverified model knowledge, to be re-derived if a fork is used; (4) **weight-only** W4/W6/W8 with FP16 activations and KV cache (the brief is silent, and RTN-vs-GPTQ is a weight-rounding contrast \\u2014 W4A4 would be a different experiment); (5) WikiText-2 as primary ppl set; (6) lm-eval-harness with the listed battery and my shot counts; (7) non-rotated RTN/GPTQ baselines treated as **required**, not optional; (8) BF16/FP16 reference obtainable; (9) calibration on C4 128\\u00d74096 identical across all cells, notwithstanding the base-style-C4-vs-instruct-model mismatch; (10) chat-template formatting fixed across cells.\\n\\nOpen choices needing your decision: (a) scope \\u2014 accept the 2\\u00d72\\u00d73 (+R\\u2032) expansion vs the literal 2\\u00d73; (b) which Hadamard-for-96 route (block-diag H\\u2083\\u2082 vs dense Had(96)); (c) is a LLaMA positive control in scope (it is what makes \\\"generalizes\\\" measurable); (d) full battery vs T1/T2 tiering; (e) an explicit quantitative success criterion for \\\"generalizes well\\\" (the brief does not define one \\u2014 I propose: relative ppl degradation at matched bits vs the LLaMA control, plus persistence of the rotation\\u00d7algorithm interaction sign); (f) whether W4A16 vs W4A4 matters to you. I'd also like to confirm the 2-core constraint, since the box reports 224.\", \"evidence\": \"All environment claims are from executed probes in this session; code-architecture claims are model knowledge of upstream QuaRot, explicitly not inspected (repo absent).\\n\\nVERIFIED BY EXECUTION:\\n- `ls -laR /workspace` \\u2192 only `task.json` (499 B); `git status` \\u2192 \\\"not a git repository\\\". task.json contents: question text + \\\"documents\\\": {\\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"}, datasets: [], gpu_enabled: false.\\n- `find / -xdev -iname '*quarot*' -o -iname '*gptq*' -o -iname '*phi-3*' -o -iname '*phi3*'` \\u2192 empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.safetensors' -o -name '*.gguf' -o -name '*.bin' -path '*model*'` \\u2192 empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.whl'` \\u2192 empty.\\n- `pip list` = 105 packages, all distro tooling; grep for torch|transformers|datasets|accelerate|hugging|numpy|scipy|safetensors|tokenizers|eval|ptq|sklearn \\u2192 no matches. `import torch` and `import numpy` \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError.\\n- Network: socket.create_connection(('pypi.org',443)) \\u2192 gaierror \\\"[Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution\\\"; `pip install numpy` \\u2192 fails (FileNotFoundError inside pip); no /etc/pip.conf. `ls -la ~/.cache` \\u2192 No such file; /home/actor empty. /tmp empty.\\n- Directories /opt /srv /data /models /mnt /media /shared /research: none exist. /usr/local/share has only ca-certificates, fonts, man, sgml, xml.\\n- `nproc`=224; `os.sched_getaffinity(0)`=224; `taskset -pc` \\u2192 \\\"0-223\\\"; no /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max. CPU: Intel Xeon Platinum 8570. `free -g`: 2011 GB total, 1935 available, 0 swap.\\n- `df`: /workspace = 1.0T, 1018G used, 6.2G avail, 100%; /tmp tmpfs 1006G free. 100 MB write probe to /workspace succeeded (space is tight but writable).\\n- /usr/bin contains gcc, gcc-15, g++, g++-15, cc, make, git, git-lfs, curl, wget; no cmake, no nvcc.\\n\\nUNVERIFIED / REPO-KNOWLEDGE-BASED (flagged as such in the answer): upstream QuaRot layout (main.py flags, models/llama.py + llama_gptq.py copies, utils/quarot_utils.py rotate_model/merge_ln/find_layers key dicts, utils/hadamard_matrix.py power-of-two assertion, utils/gptq_utils, C4/ptb calibration); Phi-3-mini config values (hidden 3072, intermediate 8192, 32 layers/32 heads, head_dim 96, num_key_value_heads 32, vocab 32064, longrope, use_mlp_bias false, fused qkv_proj/gate_up_proj, possible tied embeddings).\", \"assumptions\": [\"No experiment has been run; this is design only. The task itself states 'repositories and compute are not required', and the container has no ML stack, no weights, no datasets and no network, so nothing here is executable.\", \"Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct weights and config would be obtainable on a different (non-sandbox) execution host with network/GPU.\", \"The intended codebase is upstream astone3207/QuaRot (NeurIPS 2024 release); all LLaMA-specificity findings are model knowledge about that repo, not inspection, since the repo is absent from /workspace.\", \"Phi-3-mini config values cited (head_dim 96, num_key_value_heads=32, hidden 3072, intermediate 8192, vocab 32064, longrope, fused qkv/gate_up, possible tied embeddings) are from memory of the release config and must be verified against config.json before implementation.\", \"Weight-only quantization is intended: W4/W6/W8 with FP16 activations and FP16 KV cache. The brief does not state this; W4A4 would be a different experiment.\", \"WikiText-2 test split is the perplexity corpus (brief is silent; QuaRot also reports PTB/C4).\", \"lm-evaluation-harness (v0.4.x) is the zero-shot harness, with the task battery and shot counts I proposed; the brief does not name any suite.\", \"Non-rotated RTN and non-rotated GPTQ baselines are in scope and are required, not optional - without crossing rotation with algorithm the 2x3 cannot answer the question.\", \"An FP16/BF16 Phi-3 reference run is available and is used both as the degradation anchor and as the exactness gate for the rotation port.\", \"Calibration uses C4, 128 samples x 4096 tokens, identical across all cells; the base-C4 vs instruct-model text-style mismatch is accepted but held constant.\", \"The '2 cores effectively usable' limit is a scheduler policy, not something observable in this container (which reports 224 CPUs); throughput estimates are conditioned on it.\", \"The brief's premise that Phi-3-mini differs from LLaMA via GQA ratio appears incorrect (kv_heads=32 => plain MHA); head_dim=96 and non-power-of-two hidden=3072 are the real Hadamard-breaking deltas.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether the target QuaRot code is upstream or an internal fork - the adaptation checklist (models/phi3.py port, find_layers key sets, fused-projection handling) must be re-derived from the actual tree once available.\", \"Which Hadamard-for-head_dim-96 route to take: block-diagonal H32x3 (fast, weaker mixing) vs a dense shipped Had(96) (stronger mixing, needs a verified construction/source). This is a consequential choice for the headline claim.\", \"Whether the 'generalizes well' criterion should be defined at all, and if so against what reference (proposed: matched-bit relative ppl degradation vs a LLaMA-3-8B control plus persistence of the rotation x algorithm interaction sign). The brief defines nothing.\", \"Whether a LLaMA positive control is in budget - without it, 'generalization' has no baseline and port bugs cannot be distinguished from a genuine Phi-3 finding.\", \"Whether the full zero-shot battery is affordable on CPU; my tiering (25% paired subsamples for all cells, full battery only at 4-bit + reference) is a budget-driven compromise that halves per-task power and must be analyzed with McNemar paired tests.\", \"Disk: /workspace has only ~6 GB free, so any real run needs /tmp tmpfs or a larger volume; unverified whether that holds on the execution host.\", \"Tied embeddings on Phi-3-mini (unverified) would change how the residual-stream rotation is folded and whether lm_head can stay in FP16 cleanly.\", \"Whether Phi-3's attention scaling / longrope mscale settings in a given transformers version alter the FP16 reference ppl, which would silently confound all deltas unless one modeling path is pinned.\", \"The effective core count on the real execution host, and hence whether the CPU-only tiering above is even sufficient.\"], \"summary\": \"Inspect empty offline sandbox and propose 2x2x3 QuaRot-on-Phi3 design plan\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-ec77fb0f-e6cc-4318-93f6-aeef2c481959", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Inspect empty offline sandbox and propose 2x2x3 QuaRot-on-Phi3 design plan", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
