{"id": "ef0cce82-3300-4840-93b4-08c1b47919b7", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T17:57:40.044141", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "5fc52da4-8925-44a5-a058-a1ad2b19fd4c", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Now write the full design-only deliverable. Workspace left clean (only task.json). Good.\n\nLet me write it comprehensively but organized. Include:\n\n0. Status statement (design-only; no numbers).\n1. Pre-flight verification checklist (must-run before anything).\n2. Model/rotation adaptation spec (the port).\n3. Cell matrix with inference-per-cell.\n4. Evaluation protocol.\n5. Seeds/repeats/variance sources.\n6. Statistical analysis plan with pre-registered headlines + quantitative criteria + disconfirming conditions.\n7. Feasibility & tiering with T0 gate and failure path; measured vs assumed.\n8. Assumptions vs sources table.\n9. Limitations.\n10. Reporting plan / deliverable artifacts.\n\nBe careful: no invented numbers. Throughput numbers must be labeled as assumed ranges, with the derived hours labeled as \"arithmetic under assumed throughput bands\", which is fine (not measured outcomes of the experiment).\n\nDefine quantitative criteria:\n\nGeneralization headline (cross-model, matched bits):\n- Δppl_rel(cell, M) = (ppl_M(cell) − ppl_M(BF16)) / ppl_M(BF16).\n- \"Generalizes well\" iff, at 4-bit on Phi-3: (a) QuaRot reduces degradation vs matched non-rotated control for both algorithms: Δppl_rel^Phi3(QuaRot-X) < Δppl_rel^Phi3(Id-X) for X∈{RTN,GPTQ}; and (b) the degradation is comparable to or better than the LLaMA control: Δppl_rel^Phi3(QuaRot-GPTQ, W4) ≤ 1.5 × Δppl_rel^LLaMA(same cell) — hmm, LLaMA-3-8B is a different model size; better anchor: absolute criterion + relative criterion. Let's define:\n  - Criterion G1 (self-consistent, model-internal): rotation helps at 4-bit for both algorithms: ΔΔppl = Δppl_rel(Id-X) − Δppl_rel(QuaRot-X) > 0 with 95% CI excluding 0 for both X, AND the monotone ordering W4 > W6 > W8 in Δppl_rel holds.\n  - Criterion G2 (cross-model, requires T3): relative benefit ratio ρ_X = Δppl_rel^Phi3(Id-X)/Δppl_rel^Phi3(QuaRot-X) vs ρ_X^LLaMA; \"generalizes comparably\" iff ρ_X^Phi3 ≥ 0.5·ρ_X^LLaMA for at least one algorithm and not <0.25 for both. Hmm, need to be careful and simple. Let me set: \"generalizes well\" = the rotation's relative benefit on Phi-3 is at least half that on the LLaMA-3-8B control at the same bits and algorithm; \"partially generalizes\" = positive but < half; \"fails to generalize\" = non-positive (rotation no better than identity) for both algorithms at 4-bit, or negative (rotation hurts).\n  - Threshold stated in absolute ppl terms too: QuaRot-GPTQ W4 on Phi-3 acceptable iff ppl within +2.0 absolute / +10% relative of BF16 — mark this as a designer-proposed practical threshold (assumption), since brief silent.\n- Also absolute: QuaRot-RTN W4 acceptable iff within +1.0 ppl? No — RTN W4 typically much worse; that's the point.\n\nMechanism headline (rotation × algorithm interaction):\n- Primary contrast I = [Δppl_rel(Id-RTN) − Δppl_rel(Id-GPTQ)] − [Δppl_rel(QuaRot-RTN) − Δppl_rel(QuaRot-GPTQ)] at 4-bit (and 6-bit).\n- Pre-registered directional hypothesis: I > 0 (GPTQ's advantage shrinks once rotation removes outliers → mechanisms partially redundant).\n- Estimated with a two-factor factorial on Δppl with calibration-subset as blocking factor; bootstrap CI (resample eval examples per cell for ppl: use a per-window/per-example bootstrap; and repeat-level for quantization stochasticity).\n- Disconfirming: I ≤ 0 with CI excluding 0 → GPTQ's benefit grows under rotation (complementary mechanisms), contradicting the QuaRot/GPTQ-FAQ reading; or interaction CI covering 0 → not identified, must not claim either way.\n\nAlso note that the primary 2×3 as reported is descriptive (no rotation main effect available), and the primary inferential content comes from the 2×2×3.\n\nZero-shot: McNemar exact test on paired per-example correctness (same example IDs across cells), Holm–Bonferroni across family of pre-registered contrasts; report n and binomial SE; never compare subsample proportions independently.\n\nPower numbers: from the calc — MDE at 25% subsample with McNemar: for discordance rate 10%: 7.9pp on openbookqa 25% (n=125)... I should present the table concisely.\n\nAlso variance entry points: calibration subset (3), GPTQ percdamp (fixed 0.01; sensitivity in a separate arm), random-rotation seed (R′ only), eval nondeterminism (none for loglikelihood; gsm8k generation → greedy, temperature 0; but CPU float nondeterminism → fix threads, seeds, deterministic kernels; note bf16 accumulation order differences across thread counts → fix thread count for all cells including BF16 reference), and tokenizer/template.\n\nCritical control detail: thread count / batch size affects bf16 accumulation → must be identical across cells and reference; otherwise numerical drift contaminates small deltas. Good addition.\n\nTiering table with what's required.\n\nAlso failure paths:\n- T0 gate failure: stop, debug port (list the diagnostic sequence: (1) rotate-no-merge vs merge, (2) per-module max |Δactivation| after each merged LN to localize, (3) check fused qkv head-aligned slicing, (4) check RoPE path identity, (5) check tied embeddings). Report gate failure; do not report grid.\n- Had(96) dense arm: only if verifiable construction available (do not assert existence).\n- If instruct-calibration arm reverses RTN/GPTQ ranking at 4-bit → the primary C4-based ranking must be reported as calibration-distribution-dependent, and the headline claim must be downgraded to \"under C4 calibration\".\n\nInclude \"which numbers measured vs assumed\" statement.\n\nAlso I need to explicitly say the design's porting spec for head_dim 96 with online H post-RoPE (no commutation constraint) and v/o offline per-head rotation, hidden G block-diag.\n\nOne more thing to flag: for the block-diag H1024×3 on hidden 3072, the residual-stream rotation G must be the *same* matrix folded consistently into all consumers/producers; block-diagonal structure means coordinate i only mixes within its 1024-block — fine mathematically; but the input embedding must be rotated by G (folded into embed_tokens... but embed_tokens excluded from quantization — folding is not quantization, so it's fine; must be careful: \"excluded from quantization\" ≠ \"not rotated\"). Also lm_head: if lm_head is tied or if it consumes the rotated residual, need to fold G^T into lm_head (keep it unquantized but rotated). Important clarity point: rotation ≠ quantization; embed/lm_head unquantized but still rotated, unless we terminate the rotated stream before lm_head, which is not possible (lm_head reads residual). So: fold G into embed_tokens output and G^T into lm_head, both kept FP16. And if tied, that breaks the tie → must untie (copy lm_head = embed @ G, embeddings stored rotated) and verify that untying+rotating reproduces BF16 ppl exactly (part of the exactness gate). Nice — that's a real, sharp design detail that strengthens the exactness gate.\n\nAlso note RMSNorm merge: merging ln weight into consumers is fine for unquantized lm_head too (either merge into lm_head or keep norm unmerged for the lm_head branch; QuaRot typically merges all; keep lm_head branch un-merged? For exactness either is fine as long as verified.)\n\nLet me write it up now. Keep headers, be complete but avoid bloat. Include the tables computed.\n\nWord on seeds: seed=1337 base; calibration subsets drawn from C4 train with seeds 101/102/103; subsample seeds fixed; random-rotation seeds 201/202/203; torch.manual_seed fixed, OMP_NUM_THREADS fixed to the same value for every cell.\n\nAlso the \"primary 2×3 reported separately from 2×2×3\" per ruling 1: I'll have Section \"Reporting contract\".\n\nWrite it.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_stage", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b96162d2de4f3bee", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-b96162d2de4f3bee", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_stage", "arguments": "{\"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# QuaRot → Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct: full experiment design (DESIGN ONLY)\\n\\n**Status.** No experiment has been run, none can be run here, and no measured, estimated, or simulated outcome appears anywhere in this document. Every statement about the environment is from probes executed this session; every statement about model architecture, code layout, or task sizes is an **item to verify** (§1) or an **assumption** (§8). All throughput/duration figures are arithmetic under explicitly labelled assumed throughput bands, not measurements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Pre-flight verification checklist (blocking; run before anything else)\\n\\nNothing downstream is meaningful until these are checked against the real `config.json`, the real tree, and the real tasks. Present each as an open item, never as a fact.\\n\\n**A. Model config** (`microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct/config.json`, plus `generation_config.json`):\\n1. `hidden_size`, `intermediate_size`, `num_hidden_layers`, `num_attention_heads`; **`head_dim` derived as `hidden//heads`** — confirm it equals 96 and that no explicit `head_dim` field exists.\\n2. `num_key_value_heads` (expected 32 → GQA ratio 1, plain MHA; per your ruling the GQA framing is **removed** from the writeup, and this item exists only to confirm we are not silently hitting an untested `repeat_kv` path).\\n3. `vocab_size`, `eos_token_id`/`<|end|>` id, and **`tie_word_embeddings`** (drives §2.4).\\n4. `rope_scaling` (`longrope`, `short_factor`, `long_factor`, `mscale`), `original_max_position_embeddings`, `max_position_embeddings`, `attention_scaling`, any logit softcap, `rms_norm_eps`, `use_mlp_bias`, `use_sliding_window`/`sliding_window`.\\n5. **Which modeling path is pinned** — native `transformers.models.phi3` vs `trust_remote_code=True` custom code. Pick one, record its commit, use it for BF16 reference, all 12 cells, and the exactness gate. This is a confound if it varies.\\n6. Confirm fused-module layout and output widths: `model.layers.*.self_attn.qkv_proj` (out 3·hidden) and `mlp.gate_up_proj` (out 2·intermediate), `o_proj`, `down_proj`, and whether any attention/MLP bias exists (`input_layernorm`/`post_attention_layernorm` RMSNorm only?).\\n\\n**B. QuaRot tree** (all claims about it in this design are model-knowledge, unverified):\\n7. Locate the power-of-two assertion: expected in the Hadamard utility (`utils/hadamard_matrix.py`, `get_had`/`FastHadamardTransform`), asserted on matrix size. Record the exact call sites that pass a head-dim or hidden-dim size.\\n8. Locate where q/k online Hadamards are applied — specifically **confirm they are applied post-RoPE** (so HᵀH cancels exactly in the score, and no RoPE-commutation constraint exists). If instead they are applied pre-RoPE offline, §2.2 changes and the port needs a RoPE-compatible construction; this single fact gates the whole Phi-3 story.\\n9. Locate `find_layers`/key-list dispatch (`llama_attention_keys`, `llama_mlp_keys`) and the per-model modeling copies (`models/llama.py`, `models/llama_gptq.py`) to scope the `models/phi3.py` port.\\n10. Locate `merge_ln`/`fuse_ln_weight_into_proj` and `rotate_model`; confirm which modules are excluded from quantization by default and how `lm_head`/`embed_tokens` are rotated.\\n11. Confirm the RTN path (`--quant_method normal`) applies **per-channel** rounding on the already-rotated weights with no calibration, and that GPTQ consumes the same rotated weights — i.e. that rotation is genuinely upstream of both algorithms, which is what makes the 2×2×3 crossing valid.\\n12. Record pinned versions: torch, transformers (Phi-3 support landed ~4.41), `lm_eval`, and confirm they have wheels for the host Python (the sandbox's 3.14 will not do; a 3.10/3.11 env is required).\\n\\n**C. Harness**: task split sizes `n` per task, template/fewshot format, and that loglikelihood tasks are scored deterministically.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Port specification: organizing the port around head_dim 96 and hidden 3072\\n\\n### 2.1 Non-power-of-two rotation matrices (ruling 2)\\nPrimary rotation is **block-diagonal exact Hadamard, reusing the existing Walsh–Hadamard path**, which is exactly orthogonal and asserts nothing we cannot construct:\\n- head_dim 96 → `blkdiag(H₃₂, H₃₂, H₃₂)` (96 = 3·32);\\n- hidden 3072 → `blkdiag(H₁₀₂₄, H₁₀₂₄, H₁₀₂₄)` (3072 = 3·1024);\\n- intermediate 8192 → full `H₈₁₉₂` (clean, 2¹³) so the MLP-side rotation stays exactly as upstream.\\nScaling is 1/√block. Mixing within a 32- or 1024-block, never across blocks — the central compromise (§9).\\nPre-registered **sensitivity arm, 4-bit only**: dense `Had(96)` for head-dim, **conditional on a construction we can independently verify** (e.g. by brute-force checking H Hᵀ = 96 I on the host). No existence claim is made here. If no verifiable source, the arm is dropped and reported as not run.\\n**R′ arm (random orthogonal, identical placement, seeded QR)**, 4-bit, both algorithms, rotation applied at QuaRot's placements: separates placement/exactness from Hadamard-specific structure. If R′ ≈ QuaRot, any Phi-3 deficit is about placement/geometry, not Hadamard weakness at dim 96.\\n\\n### 2.2 Attention (head_dim 96)\\nPer-head rotations are block-diagonal over heads. If (item 8) q/k Hadamards are post-RoPE online, block-structure choice cannot break exactness — it can only weaken outlier mixing; that is precisely the effect R′ and the dense-96 arm measure. v/o_proj get the offline per-head rotation pair (H into `v` output side, Hᵀ into `o_proj` input side).\\n\\n### 2.3 Fused projections\\nLLaMA-shaped code rotates `q_proj/k_proj/v_proj` and `gate_proj/up_proj` independently. On Phi-3 these are `qkv_proj`/`gate_up_proj`. Port must apply head-aligned (q|k|v) and (gate|up) slices of the block-diagonal rotation to the fused weight, or un-fuse into views before rotation and re-fuse after. Harmless for GPTQ (per-module Hessian, groups along input dim); fatal for rotation folding if done naively. **Verification probe: after rotation and before quantization, the fused and un-fused implementations must agree to fp64 tolerance.**\\n\\n### 2.4 Residual stream, tie, and lm_head\\n`embed_tokens`/`lm_head` are **excluded from quantization** (ruling 4) but must still be **rotated** — the residual stream is in the rotated basis, so G is folded into the embedding output and Gᵀ into `lm_head`. \\\"Unquantized\\\" ≠ \\\"unrotated\\\"; this is the most likely place for a silent T0 failure. If `tie_word_embeddings` is true, rotation forces a **de-facto untying** (embeddings stored rotated, lm_head carrying Gᵀ); the exactness gate is what proves this was done correctly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Cell matrix, with the inference each cell buys\\n\\nCommon to all cells: Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct; weight-only W∈{4,6,8} symmetric; FP16 activations and FP16 KV cache (`a_bits=v_bits=k_bits=0`); **W4A4 explicitly out of scope**; `embed_tokens`/`lm_head` unquantized; identical calibration, identical modeling path, identical `OMP_NUM_THREADS`/batch (numerical-drift control); groupsize g=128, `percdamp`=0.01.\\n\\n### 3.1 PRIMARY reported result — literal 2×3 (ruling 1)\\n| Cell | Rotation | Algo | Bits |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Q-R4 / Q-R6 / Q-R8 | QuaRot (blkdiag-H) | RTN | 4 / 6 / 8 |\\n| Q-G4 / Q-G6 / Q-G8 | QuaRot (blkdiag-H) | GPTQ | 4 / 6 / 8 |\\nThis is the direct answer to the stated question and is **reported as a descriptive table: no rotation main effect, no rotation×algorithm interaction, is estimable from it.**\\n\\n### 3.2 REQUIRED controls — completes the 2×2×3\\n| Cell | Rotation | Algo | Bits | Inference bought |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| N-R4 / N-R6 / N-R8 | Identity | RTN | 4 / 6 / 8 | Rotation effect within RTN at each bit; whether plain RTN is competitive at 6/8-bit |\\n| N-G4 / N-G6 / N-G8 | Identity | GPTQ | 4 / 6 / 8 | Rotation effect within GPTQ; makes the R×A interaction identifiable — i.e. whether rotation and GPTQ rounding are redundant or complementary |\\n**B1** BF16 reference: ppl + full battery; anchor for every Δ.\\n**T0** Q-Gate16: QuaRot rotation, 16-bit, no quantization — exactness gate (§6.1).\\nCrossed cells give the mechanism claim; §5 reports the two analyses separately, never blended.\\n\\n### 3.3 Sensitivity / diagnostic arms\\n| Arm | Cells | Why |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| S-INST | 4-bit × {RTN,GPTQ}, **instruct-style** calibration (fixed small instruction slice) | GPTQ is calibration-distribution-sensitive, RTN largely is not; a C4-vs-instruct mismatch could **manufacture** an RTN/GPTQ ranking. **Survives budget cuts; PTB does not** (your ruling). If it reverses the C4 ranking, the primary headline is downgraded to \\\"under C4 calibration\\\". |\\n| S-GROUP | 4-bit RTN at g=128 and g=−1; GPTQ at g=−1 | Separates rounding-algorithm effect from group-wise representation effect. |\\n| S-DAMP | GPTQ W4, percdamp {0.01, 0.1, 1.0} | Guards against reading an ill-conditioned-Hessian artifact as an algorithmic effect. |\\n| S-HAD96 | dense Had(96) W4, both algos | Conditional (verifiable construction only). |\\n| S-RAND | R′ random orthogonal W4, both algos | Placement/exactness vs Hadamard structure. |\\n| D-DIAG | outlier stats per channel (max/median ratio, kurtosis, top-1% energy) pre/post rotation, per layer class; per-layer ‖ŴX−WX‖_F; Hessian condition number | Mechanism: does rotation actually isotropize Phi-3's activations the way it does LLaMA's? Cheap, high value, CPU-friendly. |\\n| T3-CTRL | **Optional:** LLaMA-3-8B (or Llama-2-7B) 4-bit QuaRot-RTN/GPTQ + Identity RTN | The only thing that makes \\\"generalizes\\\" a comparative claim, and the only way to separate a port bug from a genuine Phi-3 finding. **Optional-to-conclusion, budget-dependent, clearly marked.** |\\n| Dropped | PTB perplexity | First cut (your ruling). |\\n\\nTotal: 12 factorial + B1 + T0 + 2 (S-INST) + 3 (S-GROUP) + 2 (S-DAMP) + 2 (S-RAND) + 0–2 (S-HAD96) + 0–4 (T3-CTRL).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Evaluation protocol\\n\\n**Perplexity.** WikiText-2, test split, **4096-token non-overlapping windows, no stride**, plus the **2048-token slice** for comparability with published QuaRot/GPTQ tables. Tokenizer/template identical across cells; the exact test-token count is a verification item, not a fact (it sets the cost). Report **Δppl = ppl(cell) − ppl(BF16)** and **Δppl_rel = Δppl/ppl(BF16)** as primary quantities, raw ppl secondary; both context lengths always reported.\\n\\n**Zero-shot.** `lm-evaluation-harness`, `--model hf`, one pinned task-YAML/template family, identical `--num_fewshot` across cells. Battery: **core6** piqa, arc_easy, arc_challenge, hellaswag, winogrande, openbookqa (0-shot, loglikelihood); **extended** mmlu (5-shot), truthfulqa_mc, gsm8k (8-shot CoT, greedy/temp-0 — deliberately brittle, retained at 4-bit only). For every task record per-example correctness (not just the mean) — this is what makes §5.3 pairing possible.\\n\\n**Instruct-model formatting (consequential, fixed):** one chat-template policy for the whole grid (recommend the Phi-3 chat template with the harness's documented fewshot-as-single-message option, and record the rendered prompt verbatim in artifacts). Applied identically to BF16, rotated and non-rotated cells, so it can only shift all cells together, never a contrast.\\n\\n**Tiering (ruling 7).** **T1 = ppl (both ctx) + fixed-seed 25% paired subsample of core6** — mandatory for **all 12 cells**. **T2 = full battery, full splits** — only 4-bit cells (Q-R4, Q-G4, N-R4, N-G4) + B1 (+ S-INST cells, since they are 4-bit by construction). **T3 = optional** LLaMA control, S-HAD96, PTB.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Seeds, repeats, variance, statistics\\n\\n### 5.1 Where variance enters\\n1. **Calibration subset** — the dominant real source for GPTQ: **3 disjoint C4 subsets, 128×4096 tokens each (524,288 tokens/subset)**, seeds 101/102/103. Repeats are **paired by subset** across all cells, so cell-to-cell comparisons are within-subset.\\n2. **Rotation draw** — zero for block-diagonal Hadamard (deterministic, no seed); seeds 201/202/203 apply only to R′.\\n3. **Numerical nondeterminism** — bf16/fp32 accumulation order varies with thread count and batch size, which can exceed the effect sizes of interest. Fix `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, batch size, dtype, and kernel set identically for **all cells including BF16 and T0**; run the BF16 reference twice at different thread counts as a drift probe; if that drift exceeds the Δ of the mildest cell, report Δ with an explicit numerical floor.\\n4. **Eval sampling** — none (loglikelihood, greedy generation); the only stochasticity is the fixed-seed 25% T1 subsample, drawn once and shared by every cell.\\n5. RTN itself is deterministic given the rotated weights.\\n\\n**Repeats.** 4-bit: 3 repeats (variance and the ranking question both live here). 6/8-bit: 1 repeat, with the caveat that these cells carry no variance estimate and are therefore descriptive only.\\n\\n### 5.2 Pre-registered headline 1 — mechanism (ruling 6)\\nTwo-factor rotation × algorithm on Δppl_rel, bits analysed **separately at 4 and 6 bits**, calibration subset as a blocking factor:\\n\\n**I = [Δppl_rel(N-R) − Δppl_rel(N-G)] − [Δppl_rel(Q-R) − Δppl_rel(Q-G)]**, at each bit.\\n\\nDirectional hypothesis **I > 0**: GPTQ's advantage over RTN shrinks once rotation removes outliers, i.e. the two mechanisms are partially redundant. Estimation: paired differences within calibration subset; 95% CI by (i) subset-level resampling across the 3 repeats and (ii) a window-level bootstrap over WikiText-2 eval windows. With 3 repeats and paired-by-subset differencing, the detectable repeat-level SD is bounded — at SD 0.2 ppl the paired-difference MDE is ≈0.46 ppl, at SD 1.0 it is ≈2.3 ppl (arithmetic, assuming that SD; actual SD is a measured unknown). **Disconfirming:** CI excluding 0 on the negative side → mechanisms complementary, contradicting the redundancy reading; CI covering 0 → interaction **not identified**, and we must claim nothing either way and report the null.\\n\\n### 5.3 Pre-registered headline 2 — generalization (ruling 6)\\nTwo criteria, both quantitative, both requiring the T3 control for the second.\\n\\n**G-int (intrinsic, always available).** QuaRot transfers to Phi-3 iff, at 4-bit: (i) Δppl_rel(Q-X) < Δppl_rel(N-X) with CI excluding 0 for **both** X ∈ {RTN, GPTQ}; (ii) Δppl_rel is monotone decreasing in bits (W4 > W6 > W8) in all four rotation×algo combinations; (iii) rotation does not *hurt* at 8-bit (Δppl_rel(Q-X) ≤ Δppl_rel(N-X) + numerical floor). Practical acceptability threshold, proposed by me because the brief is silent: QuaRot-GPTQ W4 within **+10% relative** of BF16 WikiText-2 ppl.\\n\\n**G-cmp (comparative, needs T3).** Define relative benefit ρ_X = Δppl_rel^Phi3(N-X) / Δppl_rel^Phi3(Q-X), and ρ_X^LLaMA likewise at matched bits. **\\\"Generalizes well\\\" iff ρ_X^Phi3 ≥ 0.5·ρ_X^LLaMA for at least one algorithm and ρ_X^Phi3 > 1 for both.** Between 0 and 0.5·: partial generalization. **Disconfirming:** ρ_X^Phi3 ≤ 1 for both algorithms at 4-bit (rotation buys nothing), or ρ < 0.25·ρ^LLaMA (effect collapses on Phi-3), which we would attribute to the block-diagonal mixing compromise (§9) with S-RAND/S-HAD96 as the discriminators.\\n\\n**Zero-shot inference.** All contrasts are **paired McNemar** on per-example correctness between cells sharing the same example IDs (never independent-proportion tests, especially on 25% subsamples), with Holm–Bonferroni over the pre-registered contrast family. Always report task `n`, accuracy, binomial SE. Power note (arithmetic, assuming a 10% discordance rate): at the full openbookqa split (n≈500) McNemar detects ≈4.0 pp, but on its 25% subsample (n≈125) only ≈7.9 pp; hellaswag's subsample (n≈2510) still detects ≈1.8 pp. **Consequence:** openbookqa, arc_challenge and winogrande subsamples are underpowered for cell-vs-cell zero-shot contrasts by construction, and must be reported as descriptive only; the zero-shot claims rest on ppl plus the pooled core6 mean and on the T2 full-split cells.\\n\\n**Sensitivity reporting rule.** If S-INST reverses the RTN/GPTQ ordering at 4-bit relative to S-C4, the primary result carries the qualifier \\\"under C4 calibration\\\" and the calibration-distribution arm is promoted into the main table.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. T0 exactness gate and failure path (ruling 8)\\n\\n**Gate.** Q-Gate16 (rotation, 16-bit, no quantization) must reproduce the BF16 reference within a stated numerical tolerance before any grid cell is interpreted. Tolerance: **|Δppl| ≤ 0.02 absolute and ≤ 0.05% relative** on WikiText-2 at both 4096 and 2048 windows, plus per-task accuracy differences **exactly 0** on a fixed 500-example probe (a rotation is a change of basis; any accuracy change indicates a real modeling difference, not noise). This is a correctness check, not a statistical test — no tolerance for \\\"small but consistent\\\" drift.\\n\\n**If it fails, we stop and debug; we do not report grid cells.** Diagnostic order, most likely first: (1) residual-stream G folded into `embed_tokens` and Gᵀ into `lm_head`, and the tie handling of §2.4; (2) fused `qkv_proj`/`gate_up_proj` head-aligned slicing (§2.3); (3) `merge_ln` applied to the consumer set without double-folding; (4) per-head block-diagonal layout vs RoPE split-half pairing (§2.2); (5) RoPE/longrope/mscale/attention-scaling path differences between BF16 and the ported file; (6) dtype of the rotation application (fp32 vs bf16). Bisection procedure: run the gate with rotation but with `merge_ln` disabled, then module-class by module-class (attention-only, then MLP-only), localising the failing transformation before touching any quantizer. Report the gate failure as the finding; a failed gate makes all 12 cells uninterpretable, not merely uncertain.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Feasibility, resources, tiering (ruling 10)\\n\\n**Measured in this sandbox** (this session): `/workspace` = one 499-byte `task.json`, not a git repo; no torch/numpy/transformers/datasets/eval code; no weights, no HF cache, no datasets, no wheelhouse; DNS fails, `pip install` fails; Python 3.14.4; 224 CPUs visible with affinity `0-223` and no visible cgroup quota; 2011 GB RAM (~1935 available); `/workspace` 1.0 TB at 100% with **6.2 GB free**, `/tmp` tmpfs ~1006 GB; gcc/make/curl present but useless offline. **Therefore: nothing in this design can execute here.**\\n\\n**Planning bound.** The **2-effective-core limit is adopted as the binding planning assumption** because it is the value the task environment states; note it is *not* what the sandbox reports (224), which is itself an unresolved discrepancy.\\n\\n**Arithmetic under stated assumptions** (assumed, not measured: 3.8 B params, 7.64 GB bf16 weights, ~7.6 GFLOP/token, throughput band 15–100 tok/s on 2 cores):\\n- GPTQ Hessian scratch per layer ≈ 344 MB (2×3072² + 8192² fp32), processed layer-sequentially — RAM is never the constraint.\\n- Calibration: 128×4096 = 524,288 tokens ×3 subsets ×GPTQ cells.\\n- WikiText-2 ppl: cost scales with the (unverified) test token count; at 25 k tokens ≈ 6 windows, at 282 k ≈ 69 windows → 10–120 min per cell at 40 tok/s. Cheap.\\n- **Zero-shot is the binding constraint.** core6 ≈ 2.6 M prompt-tokens (assumed 150 tok/prompt), full battery ≈ 17.6 M (truthfulqa dominates via its ~104 targets/question). At 40 tok/s: core6 ≈ 18 h and the full battery ≈ 122 h **per cell** → 12 cells would be ≈215 h and ≈1469 h respectively. **This is exactly why T1 uses paired 25% subsamples and the full battery is restricted to 4-bit + reference cells.** Under this budget S-INST, S-GROUP, S-DAMP and S-RAND survive because they are 4-bit-only and cheap; PTB and T3 are what get cut.\\n- **Sensitivity to the core count:** if the host really exposes 224 cores, CPU GEMM scaling is memory-bandwidth-bound (realistically ~10–40×, not 112×), and cells parallelise embarrassibly. At even a 20× aggregate with 12 cells in parallel, T1 becomes near-free and the **full battery for all 12 cells** comes into reach; the T1/T2 split would then be replaced by \\\"T2 for everything, T3 included,\\\" and the zero-shot subsampling caveat (§5.3) disappears. Decision rule: measure one cell's tok/s before committing, then choose the tier; record the measured throughput in the artifact so the tier choice is auditable.\\n- **Disk:** `/tmp` tmpfs for weights (~7.6 GB bf16) and quantized dumps (~2.15 GB/cell at 4-bit+scale); `/workspace` (6.2 GB) for metrics JSON and per-example predictions only. Never write model artifacts to `/workspace`.\\n- **Host Python** must be 3.10/3.11, not 3.14 (item 12).\\n\\n**Reporting contract.** (a) Primary 2×3 table with Δppl/Δppl_rel/Δacc and raw values; (b) 2×2×3 table with rotation main effects and the interaction, reported separately; (c) arms table; (d) T0 gate result and measured throughput; (e) explicit \\\"design only, not executed\\\" banner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Assumptions vs sources\\n\\n| # | Statement | Status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | /workspace empty; no torch/numpy/transformers; no weights/datasets; offline; 224 CPUs, 2 TB RAM, 6.2 GB free on /workspace | **Measured this session** |\\n| 2 | 2 cores effectively usable | **Task-stated; contradicted by sandbox affinity; adopted as planning bound** |\\n| 3 | Phi-3 config (3072 / 8192 / 32×32 / head_dim 96 / kv_heads 32 / vocab 32064 / longrope / tie) | **Model-knowledge, unverified → §1.A** |\\n| 4 | QuaRot layout: power-of-two assert, post-RoPE online H, `find_layers` keys, fused-projection mismatch, models/llama.py copies | **Model-knowledge, unverified → §1.B** |\\n| 5 | Weight-only W4/W6/W8, FP16 acts+KV, embed/lm_head unquantized, W4A4 out of scope | **Your ruling 4** |\\n| 6 | blkdiag H32×3 / H1024×3 primary; Had(96) 4-bit conditional; R′ 4-bit | **Your ruling 2** |\\n| 7 | 2×3 primary + Identity-rotation RTN/GPTQ required as controls, reported separately | **Your ruling 1** |\\n| 8 | Phi-3 only subject; LLaMA-3-8B 4-bit as optional T3 positive control | **Your ruling 3** |\\n| 9 | C4 128×4096 primary calibration; instruct-style 4-bit arm required; PTB optional-first-cut | **Your ruling 5** |\\n| 10 | Interaction at 4/6-bit + matched-bit relative degradation as the two headlines, with thresholds | **Your ruling 6; thresholds' numeric values are my proposal** |\\n| 11 | WikiText-2 primary, 4096+2048 windows, lm-eval-harness battery, T1/T2 tiering, McNemar | **Your ruling 7; task list and shot counts mine; T1/T2 line chosen by me within your constraint** |\\n| 12 | T0 tolerances (0.02 abs / 0.05% rel / zero accuracy diff) | **My proposal — brief silent; tighten or relax before execution** |\\n| 13 | groupsize 128, percdamp 0.01, symmetric weights, seeds 101-103/201-203 | **My proposal — brief silent** |\\n| 14 | +10% relative acceptability threshold; ρ ≥ 0.5·ρ^LLaMA for \\\"generalizes well\\\" | **My proposal — brief silent on any success criterion** |\\n| 15 | chat-template formatting policy | **My proposal — brief silent** |\\n| 16 | 15–100 tok/s, 150 tok/prompt, task n's, WikiText-2 token count | **Assumed for costing only; measure on host, then fix tier** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Limitations\\n\\n1. **Design only.** Nothing here was run; this sandbox cannot run it (no torch, no numpy, no weights, no datasets, no network). Every quantity is a plan, a tolerance, or arithmetic on assumed constants.\\n2. **The block-diagonal mixing compromise is the central internal threat.** Because head_dim 96 and hidden 3072 are not powers of two, our \\\"QuaRot on Phi-3\\\" uses `blkdiag(H₃₂×3)` and `blkdiag(H₁₀₂₄×3)`, which mix less thoroughly than a full Hadamard and may leave outliers partly intact. A negative result on Phi-3 therefore cannot by itself distinguish \\\"QuaRot does not generalize to Phi-3\\\" from \\\"block-diagonal rotation is too weak at dim 96\\\". S-RAND and (if a verifiable Had(96) exists) S-HAD96 are the only discriminators, and S-HAD96 is conditional — this limitation may not be resolvable in this budget.\\n3. **Calibration confound for the RTN/GPTQ ranking** (S-INST exists precisely because the C4-vs-instruct mismatch could produce an artifact rather than a property of the algorithms).\\n4. **Zero-shot subsampling underpower** several core tasks by construction (§5.3); zero-shot contrasts at 6/8-bit are descriptive only.\\n5. **6/8-bit cells are single-repeated**, so absence of variance there is by design, not evidence of stability.\\n6. **Unverified substrate.** Both the Phi-3 config and every claim about QuaRot's code path are model-knowledge; §1 is blocking precisely because a wrong assumption there (esp. items 8 and 9) invalidates the port and the headline.\\n7. **Single model, single family.** One Phi-3 variant, and — per your ruling — no GQA stress and no MoE; conclusions are about Phi-3-mini's dense-MHA shape, not about \\\"non-LLaMA models\\\" generally. T3, if unfunded, removes the comparative half of the generalization claim (G-cmp) and leaves only G-int.\\n8. **Tied-embedding de-tying** (if item 3 confirms tying) makes the rotated model structurally different from the released checkpoint even at 16-bit in the parameter-tie sense; the T0 gate bounds the numerical consequence but not the interpretive caveat.\\n9. **Resource bound unresolved** (2 vs 224 cores), so the tier actually executed may differ from the tier planned; the tier decision and measured throughput must be recorded.\", \"evidence\": \"ENVIRONMENT (measured this session, all via execute_check):\\n- `ls -laR /workspace` → only task.json (499 B); `git status` → \\\"not a git repository\\\". task.json: question text, \\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\", datasets: [], gpu_enabled: false.\\n- `find / -xdev -iname '*quarot*' -o -iname '*gptq*' -o -iname '*phi-3*' -o -iname '*phi3*'` → empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.safetensors' -o -name '*.gguf' -o -name '*.bin' -path '*model*'` → empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.whl'` → empty.\\n- `import torch` / `import numpy` → ModuleNotFoundError. pip list = 105 pkgs, all distro tooling; grep torch|transformers|datasets|accelerate|numpy|scipy|tokenizers|safetensors|eval|ptq → no match.\\n- Network: socket to pypi.org:443 → gaierror \\\"Temporary failure in name resolution\\\"; `pip install numpy` fails; no /etc/pip.conf; ~/.cache absent.\\n- nproc=224, sched_getaffinity=224 (0-223), no cgroup cpu.max; Xeon Platinum 8570; free -g: 2011 total / 1935 available.\\n- df: /workspace 1.0T, 1018G used, 6.2G avail (100%); /tmp tmpfs 1006G. 100MB write probe to /workspace succeeded.\\n- /usr/bin has gcc/gcc-15, g++, cc, make, git, git-lfs, curl, wget; no cmake, no nvcc.\\n\\nARITHMETIC grounding for §2.1/§3/§7 (python3, pure arithmetic on assumed constants — no model, no data):\\n- head_dim = 3072//32 = 96; (96 & 95) != 0 → not power of two; 96 = 3*32; 3072 = 3*1024; 8192 power-of-two = True.\\n- Params ≈ 3.82 B (113.25 M/layer with fused qkv 3072x9216, o_proj, gate_up 3072x16384, down 8192x3072); bf16 = 7.64 GB; int4+scale ≈ 2.15 GB.\\n- GPTQ Hessian fp32: qkv 38 MB, gate_up 38 MB, down_proj 268 MB → ~344 MB/layer sequential. Calibration 128x4096 = 524,288 tokens.\\n- Task n's (assumed, to verify) and binomial SE at p=.5: piqa 1838/1.17pp, arc_easy 2376/1.03, arc_challenge 1172/1.46, hellaswag 10042/0.50, winogrande 1267/1.40, openbookqa 500/2.24, mmlu 14042/0.42, truthfulqa 817/1.75, gsm8k 1319/1.38. core6 n = 17,195.\\n- Prefill estimate at 150 tok/prompt (truthfulqa x104 targets): core6 ~2.6M tokens, full battery ~17.6M. At 40 tok/s: core6 17.9 h/cell, full 122.4 h/cell; x12 cells = 215 h / 1469 h. At 15 tok/s: 573 h / 3917 h.\\n- WikiText-2 ppl cost parametric: 25k tok ≈ 6 windows (10 min/cell @40 tok/s); 282k ≈ 69 windows (118 min/cell).\\n- Repeat-level MDE with 3 paired repeats: SD .2 → paired-diff SE .163, MDE .462; SD 1.0 → SE .816, MDE 2.311.\\n- McNemar vs independent MDE at 80% power (Z=2.80): e.g. n=125 → 7.9 pp vs