ence claim is made.\\\", \\\"T0 numerical tolerances (0.02 absolute / 0.05 percent relative ppl, zero accuracy change on a 500-example probe) are my proposed thresholds; the brief specifies none.\\\", \\\"Success thresholds (+10 percent relative ppl acceptability; rho >= 0.5 x rho_LLama for 'generalizes well'; interaction I>0) are my proposals; the brief defines no criterion.\\\", \\\"One fixed chat-template formatting policy and one pinned modeling path (native transformers phi3 vs trust_remote_code) apply to every cell including the BF16 reference and T0.\\\", \\\"Execution host runs Python 3.10/3.11 in a conda env; the sandbox's Python 3.14 cannot host the pinned torch/transformers stack.\\\", \\\"The LLaMA-3-8B positive control is optional-to-conclusion; if unfunded, only the intrinsic generalization criterion G-int survives.\\\"]\", \"uncertainties\": \"[\\\"Whether QuaRot applies the q/k Hadamards post-RoPE (exactness-preserving) or pre-RoPE offline - the single most consequential unknown; if pre-RoPE, the dim-96 problem becomes a RoPE-compatibility problem and section 2 must be rewritten.\\\", \\\"Whether Phi-3-mini has tied word embeddings; if tied, the residual-stream rotation forces a de-facto untying that the T0 gate bounds numerically but not interpretationally.\\\", \\\"How large the WikiText-2 test split is in Phi-3 tokens, which sets per-cell ppl cost and therefore which tier is affordable.\\\", \\\"What the actual repeat-to-repeat SD of GPTQ Δppl across calibration subsets is; the MDE figures are conditional on an assumed SD and are only known after the 4-bit repeats run.\\\", \\\"Whether a verifiable Had(96) construction is obtainable; if not, the block-diagonal-mixing confound in the limitations section cannot be separated from a genuine Phi-3 finding.\\\", \\\"Whether the instruct-calibration arm reverses the RTN/GPTQ ordering obtained under C4 - if it does, the primary headline must be qualified and the arm promoted into the main table.\\\", \\\"Real CPU throughput and scaling on the execution host (memory-bandwidth-bound), which decides whether the T1/T2 split or full-battery-for-all-cells is executed.\\\", \\\"Whether lm-evaluation-harness versions compatible with the pinned transformers expose the Phi-3 chat template consistently across all tasks; template drift across cells would confound every zero-shot delta.\\\", \\\"Whether the port of rotation folding into fused qkv_proj / gate_up_proj introduces any non-exactness beyond what the module-class bisection in the T0 failure path can localise.\\\"]\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-725b701a-6f9b-43ec-87fb-013cb6c7d670", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": null, "kind": "ActionEvent"}
