{"id": "7b96dd11-17bd-4c76-9d0f-4bf86ff5620a", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T17:59:47.770189", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "748828fc-215d-438c-bf6c-cad798a33e44", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "I mistakenly used the wrong tool name. Resubmit with end_researcher_turn.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "# QuaRot → Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct: full experiment design (DESIGN ONLY)\n\n**Status.** No experiment has been run, none can be run in this sandbox, and no measured, estimated, or simulated outcome appears anywhere in this document. Every environment statement comes from probes executed this session; every architecture/code-layout/task-size statement is an **item to verify** (§1) or an **assumption** (§8). All throughput and duration figures are arithmetic under explicitly labelled assumed constants, not measurements.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pre-flight verification checklist (blocking; run before anything else)\n\nNothing downstream is meaningful until these are checked against the real `config.json`, the real tree, and the real task definitions. Each is an open item, never a fact.\n\n**A. Model config** (`microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct/config.json` + `generation_config.json`):\n1. `hidden_size`, `intermediate_size`, `num_hidden_layers`, `num_attention_heads`; **`head_dim` derived as `hidden//heads`** — confirm 96 and that no explicit `head_dim` field exists.\n2. `num_key_value_heads` (expected 32 → GQA ratio 1, plain MHA). Per your ruling the GQA framing is **removed from the writeup**; this item exists only to confirm we are not silently relying on an untested `repeat_kv` path.\n3. `vocab_size`, `eos_token_id`/`<|end|>` id, and **`tie_word_embeddings`** (drives §2.4).\n4. `rope_scaling` (`longrope`, `short_factor`, `long_factor`, `mscale`), `original_max_position_embeddings`, `max_position_embeddings`, `attention_scaling`, any logit softcap, `rms_norm_eps`, `use_mlp_bias`, `use_sliding_window`/`sliding_window`.\n5. **Which modeling path is pinned** — native `transformers.models.phi3` vs `trust_remote_code=True` custom code. Pick one, record its commit, use it for the BF16 reference, all 12 cells, and the exactness gate. A mismatch here is a silent confound.\n6. Confirm fused-module layout and widths: `self_attn.qkv_proj` (out 3·hidden), `self_attn.o_proj`, `mlp.gate_up_proj` (out 2·intermediate), `mlp.down_proj`, and whether any attention/MLP **bias** exists (RMSNorm in `input_layernorm`/`post_attention_layernorm` only?).\n\n**B. QuaRot tree** (all claims about it in this design are model-knowledge, unverified):\n7. Locate the power-of-two assertion — expected in the Hadamard utility (`utils/hadamard_matrix.py`, `get_had`/`FastHadamardTransform`) asserting on matrix size — and record every call site that passes a head-dim or hidden-dim size.\n8. Locate where the q/k Hadamards are applied and **confirm they are applied post-RoPE**, so HᵀH cancels exactly in the score and no RoPE-commutation constraint exists. If they are instead applied pre-RoPE offline, §2.2 changes completely and the port needs a RoPE-compatible construction; this single fact gates the whole Phi-3 story.\n9. Locate the module-selection dispatch (`llama_attention_keys`, `llama_mlp_keys` in `find_layers`) and the per-model modeling copies (`models/llama.py`, `models/llama_gptq.py`) to scope the `models/phi3.py` port.\n10. Locate `merge_ln`/`fuse_ln_weight_into_proj` and `rotate_model`; confirm which modules are excluded from quantization by default and how `lm_head`/`embed_tokens` are treated.\n11. Confirm the RTN path (`--quant_method normal`) rounds the **already-rotated** weights per channel with no calibration, and that GPTQ consumes the same rotated weights — i.e. rotation is genuinely upstream of both algorithms, which is what makes the 2×2×3 crossing valid.\n12. Record pinned versions (torch, transformers — Phi-3 support landed ~4.41, `lm_eval`) and confirm wheels exist for the host Python. The sandbox's **3.14 will not do**; a 3.10/3.11 env is required.\n\n**C. Harness**: per-task split sizes `n`, template/fewshot format, and confirmation that loglikelihood tasks score deterministically.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Port specification: organizing the port around head_dim 96 and hidden 3072\n\n### 2.1 Non-power-of-two rotations (your ruling 2)\nPrimary rotation = **block-diagonal exact Hadamard reusing the existing Walsh–Hadamard path** — exactly orthogonal, and asserting nothing we cannot construct:\n- head_dim 96 → `blkdiag(H₃₂, H₃₂, H₃₂)` (96 = 3·32);\n- hidden 3072 → `blkdiag(H₁₀₂₄, H₁₀₂₄, H₁₀₂₄)` (3072 = 3·1024);\n- intermediate 8192 → full `H₈₁₉₂` (clean, 2¹³), so the MLP-side rotation stays exactly as upstream.\n\nScaling 1/√block. Mixing occurs within a 32- or 1024-block, never across blocks — the central compromise (§9).\n**Pre-registered sensitivity arm, 4-bit only:** dense `Had(96)` for the head dim, **conditional on a construction we can independently verify on the host** (brute-force check `H Hᵀ = 96 I`). No existence claim is made here. If nothing verifiable is available, the arm is dropped and reported as not run.\n**R′ arm (seeded random orthogonal, identical placement):** 4-bit, both algorithms. Separates placement/exactness from Hadamard-specific structure: if R′ ≈ QuaRot, any Phi-3 deficit is about placement/geometry rather than Hadamard weakness at dim 96.\n\n### 2.2 Attention (head_dim 96)\nPer-head rotations stay block-diagonal over heads. If item 8 confirms post-RoPE online application, the *block structure* choice cannot break exactness — it can only weaken outlier mixing, which is exactly what S-RAND and S-HAD96 measure. v/o_proj take the offline per-head pair (H on the v output side, Hᵀ on the o_proj input side).\n\n### 2.3 Fused projections\nLLaMA-shaped code rotates `q_proj/k_proj/v_proj` and `gate_proj/up_proj` independently; Phi-3 exposes `qkv_proj`/`gate_up_proj`. The port must apply head-aligned (q|k|v) and (gate|up) slices of the block-diagonal rotation to the fused weight, or un-fuse into views before rotation and re-fuse after. Harmless for GPTQ (per-module Hessian, groups along the input dim); fatal for rotation folding if done naively. **Verification probe:** after rotation, before any quantization, the fused and un-fused implementations must agree to fp64 tolerance.\n\n### 2.4 Residual stream, tying, lm_head\n`embed_tokens`/`lm_head` are **excluded from quantization** (your ruling 4) but must still be **rotated** — the residual stream lives in the rotated basis, so G is folded into the embedding output and Gᵀ into `lm_head`. \"Unquantized\" ≠ \"unrotated\"; this is the most likely site of a silent T0 failure. If `tie_word_embeddings` is true, rotation forces a **de-facto untying** (rotated embeddings, lm_head carrying Gᵀ); the exactness gate is what proves this was done correctly.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Cell matrix, with the inference each cell buys\n\nCommon to all cells: Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct; weight-only W∈{4,6,8} symmetric; FP16 activations and FP16 KV cache (`a_bits=v_bits=k_bits=0`); **W4A4 explicitly out of scope**; `embed_tokens`/`lm_head` unquantized; identical calibration, modeling path, `OMP_NUM_THREADS` and batch size (numerical-drift control); groupsize g=128, `percdamp`=0.01.\n\n### 3.1 PRIMARY reported result — the literal 2×3 (your ruling 1)\n| Cell | Rotation | Algo | Bits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Q-R4 / Q-R6 / Q-R8 | QuaRot (blkdiag-H) | RTN | 4 / 6 / 8 |\n| Q-G4 / Q-G6 / Q-G8 | QuaRot (blkdiag-H) | GPTQ | 4 / 6 / 8 |\n\nReported as the direct answer to the stated question and, explicitly, **as a descriptive table: no rotation main effect and no rotation×algorithm interaction is estimable from it.**\n\n### 3.2 REQUIRED controls — completing the 2×2×3\n| Cell | Rotation | Algo | Bits | Inference bought |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| N-R4 / N-R6 / N-R8 | Identity | RTN | 4 / 6 / 8 | Rotation effect within RTN at each bit; whether unrotated RTN is already competitive at 6/8-bit |\n| N-G4 / N-G6 / N-G8 | Identity | GPTQ | 4 / 6 / 8 | Rotation effect within GPTQ; makes R×A identifiable, i.e. whether rotation and GPTQ rounding are redundant or complementary |\n\n**B1** BF16 reference (ppl + full battery) — the anchor for every Δ.\n**T0** Q-Gate16 — QuaRot rotation, 16-bit, no quantization (§6).\n§5 reports the 2×3 and the 2×2×3 analyses **separately, never blended.**\n\n### 3.3 Sensitivity / diagnostic arms\n| Arm | Cells | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **S-INST** | 4-bit × {RTN, GPTQ} with an **instruct-style** calibration set (fixed small instruction slice) | GPTQ is calibration-distribution-sensitive, RTN largely is not; the C4-vs-instruct mismatch could **manufacture** an RTN/GPTQ ranking. **Survives budget cuts; PTB does not** (your ruling 5). If it reverses the C4 ordering, the primary headline is downgraded to \"under C4 calibration\". |\n| S-GROUP | 4-bit: RTN at g=128 and g=−1; GPTQ at g=−1 | Separates the rounding-algorithm effect from the group-wise-representation effect. |\n| S-DAMP | GPTQ W4, percdamp {0.01, 0.1, 1.0} | Prevents reading an ill-conditioned-Hessian artifact as an algorithmic effect. |\n| S-HAD96 | dense Had(96), W4, both algos | **Conditional** on a verifiable construction only. |\n| S-RAND | R′ random orthogonal, W4, both algos | Placement/exactness vs Hadamard structure. |\n| D-DIAG | per-channel activation max/median ratio, kurtosis, top-1%-energy **pre vs post rotation** per layer class; per-layer ‖ŴX−WX‖_F; Hessian condition number | Mechanism: does rotation actually isotropize Phi-3 activations the way it does LLaMA's? Cheap and CPU-friendly. |\n| **T3-CTRL** | **Optional:** LLaMA-3-8B (or Llama-2-7B) 4-bit QuaRot-RTN/GPTQ + Identity-RTN | The only thing that makes \"generalizes\" a comparative claim, and the only way to separate a port bug from a genuine Phi-3 finding. **Optional-to-conclusion, budget-dependent, clearly marked** (your ruling 3). |\n| Dropped | PTB perplexity | First cut (your ruling 5). |\n\nTotals: 12 factorial + B1 + T0 + 2 (S-INST) + 3 (S-GROUP) + 2 (S-DAMP) + 2 (S-RAND) + 0–2 (S-HAD96) + 0–4 (T3-CTRL).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Evaluation protocol\n\n**Perplexity.** WikiText-2 test split, **4096-token non-overlapping windows, no stride**, plus the **2048-token slice** for comparability with published QuaRot/GPTQ tables. Tokenizer and template identical across cells. The exact test token count is a verification item, not a fact — it sets the per-cell cost. Primary quantities are **Δppl = ppl(cell) − ppl(BF16)** and **Δppl_rel = Δppl / ppl(BF16)**; raw ppl secondary; both context lengths always reported.\n\n**Zero-shot.** `lm-evaluation-harness`, `--model hf`, one pinned task-YAML/template family, identical `--num_fewshot` across cells. **core6**: piqa, arc_easy, arc_challenge, hellaswag, winogrande, openbookqa (0-shot, loglikelihood). **Extended**: mmlu (5-shot), truthfulqa_mc, gsm8k (8-shot CoT, greedy/temp-0 — deliberately brittle; 4-bit cells only). Record **per-example correctness**, not just means — that is what makes §5.3 pairing possible.\n\n**Instruct-model formatting (consequential, fixed once).** One chat-template policy for the entire grid (recommend the Phi-3 chat template with the harness's documented fewshot-as-single-message option; store the rendered prompt verbatim in the artifacts). Applied identically to BF16, rotated and unrotated cells, so it can shift all cells together but cannot create a contrast.\n\n**Tiering (your ruling 7).** **T1** = ppl at both contexts + fixed-seed **25% paired subsample of core6** — mandatory for **all 12 cells**. **T2** = full battery, full splits — 4-bit cells (Q-R4, Q-G4, N-R4, N-G4) + B1 (+ S-INST cells, which are 4-bit by construction). **T3** = optional LLaMA control, S-HAD96, PTB.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Seeds, repeats, variance, statistics\n\n### 5.1 Where variance enters\n1. **Calibration subset** — the dominant real source for GPTQ: **3 disjoint C4 subsets, 128×4096 = 524,288 tokens each**, seeds 101/102/103. Repeats are **paired by subset across all cells**, so every cell-to-cell comparison is within-subset.\n2. **Rotation draw** — zero for block-diagonal Hadamard (deterministic, no seed); seeds 201/202/203 apply only to R′.\n3. **Numerical nondeterminism** — bf16/fp32 accumulation order varies with thread count and batch size and can exceed the effect sizes of interest. Fix `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, batch size, dtype and kernel set identically for **all cells including BF16 and T0**; run the BF16 reference twice at different thread counts as a drift probe. If that drift exceeds the smallest Δ in the grid, report Δ against an explicit numerical floor rather than claiming effects beneath it.\n4. **Eval sampling** — none (loglikelihood, greedy generation); the only stochasticity is the fixed-seed 25% T1 subsample, drawn once and shared by every cell.\n5. RTN itself is deterministic given the rotated weights.\n\n**Repeats.** 4-bit: 3 repeats (variance and the ranking question both live here). 6/8-bit: 1 repeat, flagged as **descriptive only, with no variance estimate by design**.\n\n### 5.2 Pre-registered headline 1 — mechanism (your ruling 6)\nTwo-factor rotation × algorithm on Δppl_rel, analysed **separately at 4 and 6 bits**, calibration subset as blocking factor:\n\n**I = [Δppl_rel(N-R) − Δppl_rel(N-G)] − [Δppl_rel(Q-R) − Δppl_rel(Q-G)]** at each bit.\n\nDirectional hypothesis **I > 0**: GPTQ's advantage over RTN shrinks once rotation removes outliers, i.e. the mechanisms are partially redundant. Estimated on differences paired by calibration subset, with 95% CIs from (i) subset-level resampling over the 3 repeats and (ii) a window-level bootstrap over WikiText-2 eval windows. Conditional on an assumed repeat SD, the paired-difference MDE with 3 repeats is ≈0.46 ppl at SD 0.2 and ≈2.3 ppl at SD 1.0 (arithmetic; the true SD is unknown until run). **Disconfirming:** CI excluding 0 on the negative side → mechanisms complementary, contradicting the redundancy reading; CI covering 0 → interaction **not identified**, and we claim nothing either way and report the null.\n\n### 5.3 Pre-registered headline 2 — generalization (your ruling 6)\n**G-int (intrinsic, always available).** QuaRot transfers to Phi-3 iff at 4-bit: (i) Δppl_rel(Q-X) < Δppl_rel(N-X) with CI excluding 0 for **both** X ∈ {RTN, GPTQ}; (ii) Δppl_rel monotone in bits (W4 > W6 > W8) in all four rotation×algo combinations; (iii) rotation does not *hurt* at 8-bit (Δppl_rel(Q-X) ≤ Δppl_rel(N-X) + numerical floor). Proposed practical acceptability (mine, since the brief is silent): QuaRot-GPTQ W4 within **+10% relative** of BF16 WikiText-2 ppl.\n\n**G-cmp (comparative, needs T3).** Relative benefit ρ_X = Δppl_rel^Phi3(N-X) / Δppl_rel^Phi3(Q-X), and ρ_X^LLaMA at matched bits. **\"Generalizes well\" iff ρ_X^Phi3 ≥ 0.5·ρ_X^LLaMA for at least one algorithm and ρ_X^Phi3 > 1 for both.** Between 0 and 0.5·: partial. **Disconfirming:** ρ_X^Phi3 ≤ 1 for both algorithms at 4-bit (rotation buys nothing on Phi-3), or ρ < 0.25·ρ^LLaMA (effect collapses), which we would attribute to the block-diagonal mixing compromise (§9), using S-RAND/S-HAD96 as discriminators.\n\n**Zero-shot inference.** All contrasts are **paired McNemar** on per-example correctness between cells sharing example IDs — never independent-proportion tests, especially not on 25% subsamples — with Holm–Bonferroni over the pre-registered contrast family. Always report task `n`, accuracy, and binomial SE. Power note (arithmetic at an assumed 10% discordance rate): at the full openbookqa split (n≈500) McNemar detects ≈4.0 pp, but on its 25% subsample (n≈125) only ≈7.9 pp, whereas hellaswag's subsample (n≈2510) still detects ≈1.8 pp. **Consequence:** openbookqa, arc_challenge and winogrande subsamples are underpowered for cell-vs-cell zero-shot contrasts **by construction** and are reported as descriptive only; zero-shot claims rest on ppl, the pooled core6 mean, and the T2 full-split cells.\n\n**Sensitivity reporting rule.** If S-INST reverses the RTN/GPTQ ordering obtained under C4, the primary result is qualified \"under C4 calibration\" and the calibration arm is promoted into the main table.\n\n---\n\n## 6. T0 exactness gate and failure path (your ruling 8)\n\n**Gate.** Q-Gate16 (rotation, 16-bit, no quantization) must reproduce the BF16 reference within stated tolerance **before any grid cell is interpreted**: **|Δppl| ≤ 0.02 absolute and ≤ 0.05% relative** on WikiText-2 at both 4096 and 2048 windows, plus **exactly zero** per-task accuracy differences on a fixed 500-example probe. A rotation is a change of basis, so any consistent accuracy change indicates a real modeling difference, not noise.\n\n**If it fails we stop and debug; we do not report grid cells.** Diagnostic order, most likely first: (1) G folded into `embed_tokens` / Gᵀ into `lm_head`, and the tie handling of §2.4; (2) fused `qkv_proj`/`gate_up_proj` head-aligned slicing (§2.3); (3) `merge_ln` consumer set without double-folding; (4) per-head block layout vs RoPE split-half pairing (§2.2); (5) RoPE/longrope/mscale/attention-scaling differences between BF16 and the ported file; (6) dtype of the rotation application (fp32 vs bf16). Bisection: run the gate with `merge_ln` disabled, then module-class by module-class (attention-only, then MLP-only), localising the failing transformation before touching a quantizer. A failed gate makes all 12 cells uninterpretable, not merely uncertain — the gate failure *is* the finding in that branch.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Feasibility, resources, tiering (your ruling 10)\n\n**Measured in this sandbox this session:** `/workspace` contains one 499-byte `task.json`, not a git repo; no torch/numpy/transformers/datasets/eval code; no weights, no HF cache, no datasets, no wheelhouse; DNS fails and `pip install` fails; Python 3.14.4; 224 CPUs visible with affinity `0-223` and no visible cgroup quota; 2011 GB RAM (~1935 available); `/workspace` 1.0 TB at 100% with **6.2 GB free**; `/tmp` tmpfs ~1006 GB; gcc/make/curl present but useless offline. **Nothing in this design can execute here.**\n\n**Planning bound.** The **2-effective-core limit is adopted as the binding planning assumption** because that is what the task environment states; it is *not* what the sandbox reports (224), and the discrepancy is unresolved.\n\n**Arithmetic under stated assumptions** (assumed, not measured: 3.8 B params, 7.64 GB bf16 weights, ~7.6 GFLOP/token, a throughput band of 15–100 tok/s on 2 cores):\n- GPTQ Hessian scratch ≈ **344 MB per layer** (2×3072² + 8192² fp32, layer-sequential) — RAM is never the constraint; 8192² Cholesky solves are seconds, forward passes dominate.\n- Calibration: 524,288 tokens per subset × 3 subsets × GPTQ cells.\n- WikiText-2 ppl cost scales with the (unverified) test token count: ~25 k tokens ≈ 6 windows; ~282 k ≈ 69 windows → 10–120 min per cell at 40 tok/s. Cheap.\n- **Zero-shot is the binding constraint.** core6 ≈ 2.6 M prompt-tokens (assumed 150 tok/prompt), full battery ≈ 17.6 M (truthfulqa dominates via ~104 targets/question). At 40 tok/s: core6 ≈ **18 h per cell**, full battery ≈ **122 h per cell** → 12 cells ≈ **215 h** and **1469 h** respectively (at 15 tok/s: 573 h / 3917 h). This is precisely why T1 uses paired 25% subsamples and the full battery is restricted to 4-bit + references, and why S-INST/S-GROUP/S-DAMP/S-RAND survive (4-bit-only, cheap) while PTB and T3 are what get cut.\n- **Sensitivity to core count:** if the host really exposes 224 cores, CPU GEMM scaling is memory-bandwidth-bound (realistically ~10–40× aggregate, not 112×) and cells parallelise embarrassibly. At ~20× aggregate with 12 cells in parallel, T1 becomes near-free and the **full battery for all 12 cells** comes into reach; the T1/T2 split would then be replaced by \"T2 for everything, T3 included,\" and the §5.3 subsampling caveat disappears. Decision rule: measure one cell's tok/s before committing, then choose the tier, and record the measured throughput in the artifact so the tier choice is auditable.\n- **Disk:** `/tmp` tmpfs for bf16 weights (~7.6 GB) and quantized dumps (~2.15 GB per 4-bit cell); `/workspace` (6.2 GB free) for metrics JSON and per-example predictions only. Never write model artifacts to `/workspace`.\n\n**Reporting contract.** (a) primary 2×3 table with Δppl / Δppl_rel / Δacc and raw values; (b) the 2×2×3 table with rotation main effects and the interaction, reported separately; (c) arms table; (d) T0 gate result and measured throughput; (e) an explicit \"design only, not executed\" banner on every table.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Assumptions vs sources\n\n| # | Statement | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | /workspace holds only task.json; no torch/numpy/transformers; no weights/datasets; offline; 224 CPUs, 2 TB RAM, 6.2 GB free on /workspace | **Measured this session** |\n| 2 | 2 cores effectively usable | **Task-stated; contradicted by sandbox affinity; adopted as planning bound** |\n| 3 | Phi-3 config (3072 / 8192 / 32×32 / head_dim 96 / kv_heads 32 / vocab 32064 / longrope / tie) | **Model-knowledge, unverified → §1.A** |\n| 4 | QuaRot layout: power-of-two assert, post-RoPE online H, `find_layers` keys, fused-module mismatch, `models/llama.py` copies, RTN = `--quant_method normal` | **Model-knowledge, unverified → §1.B** |\n| 5 | Weight-only W4/W6/W8, FP16 acts+KV, embed/lm_head unquantized, W4A4 out of scope | **Your ruling 4** |\n| 6 | blkdiag H32×3 / H1024×3 primary; Had(96) 4-bit conditional; R′ 4-bit | **Your ruling 2** |\n| 7 | 2×3 primary, Identity-rotation RTN/GPTQ required as controls, reported separately | **Your ruling 1** |\n| 8 | Phi-3 the only subject; LLaMA-3-8B 4-bit as optional T3 positive control | **Your ruling 3** |\n| 9 | C4 128×4096 primary; instruct-style 4-bit arm required; PTB optional, first cut | **Your ruling 5** |\n| 10 | Interaction at 4/6-bit and matched-bit relative degradation as the two headlines | **Your ruling 6; the numeric thresholds are my proposal** |\n| 11 | WikiText-2 primary, 4096+2048 windows, lm-eval-harness battery, T1/T2 tiering, McNemar | **Your ruling 7; task list, shot counts and the exact T1/T2 line are mine within your constraint** |\n| 12 | T0 tolerances (0.02 abs / 0.05% rel / zero accuracy diff) | **My proposal — brief silent** |\n| 13 | groupsize 128, percdamp 0.01, symmetric weights, seeds 101-103/201-203 | **My proposal — brief silent** |\n| 14 | +10% relative acceptability; ρ ≥ 0.5·ρ^LLaMA for \"generalizes well\" | **My proposal — brief gives no success criterion** |\n| 15 | One chat-template policy | **My proposal — brief silent** |\n| 16 | 15–100 tok/s, 150 tok/prompt, task n's, WikiText-2 token count | **Costing assumptions; measure on host, then fix the tier** |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Limitations\n\n1. **Design only.** Nothing was run and this sandbox cannot run it (no torch, no numpy, no weights, no datasets, no network). Every quantity here is a plan, a tolerance, or arithmetic on assumed constants.\n2. **The block-diagonal mixing compromise is the central internal threat.** Because head_dim 96 and hidden 3072 are not powers of two, \"QuaRot on Phi-3\" here means `blkdiag(H₃₂×3)` and `blkdiag(H₁₀₂₄×3)`, which mix less thoroughly than a full Hadamard and may leave outliers partly intact. A negative Phi-3 result therefore cannot by itself distinguish \"QuaRot does not generalize to Phi-3\" from \"block-diagonal rotation is too weak at dim 96\". S-RAND and (only if a verifiable Had(96) exists) S-HAD96 are the discriminators, and S-HAD96 is conditional — this limitation may not be resolvable within budget.\n3. **Calibration confound** for the RTN/GPTQ ranking; S-INST exists precisely because a C4-vs-instruct mismatch could produce an artifact rather than a property of the algorithms.\n4. **Zero-shot subsampling underpower** affects several core tasks by construction (§5.3); zero-shot contrasts at 6/8-bit are descriptive only.\n5. **6/8-bit cells are single-repeated** — absence of variance there is by design, not evidence of stability.\n6. **Unverified substrate.** Both the Phi-3 config and every QuaRot code claim are model-knowledge; §1 is blocking because a wrong assumption there (especially items 8 and 9) invalidates the port and the headline.\n7. **Single model, single shape.** One Phi-3 variant, no GQA stress (ratio 1) and no MoE; conclusions concern Phi-3-mini's dense-MHA shape, not \"non-LLaMA models\" generally. If T3 is unfunded, the comparative half of the generalization claim (G-cmp) is lost and only G-int survives.\n8. **Tied-embedding de-tying** (if item 3 confirms tying) makes the rotated model structurally different from the released checkpoint even at 16-bit in the parameter-tie sense; T0 bounds the numerical consequence, not the interpretive caveat.\n9. **Resource bound unresolved** (2 vs 224 cores), so the executed tier may differ from the planned tier; the decision and the measured throughput must be recorded with the results.", "evidence": "ENVIRONMENT (measured this session via execute_check):\n- `ls -laR /workspace` → only task.json (499 B); `git status` → \"not a git repository\". task.json contents: the question, \"track.md\": \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\", datasets: [], gpu_enabled: false, cpu_affinity_count: 224.\n- `find / -xdev -iname '*quarot*' -o -iname '*gptq*' -o -iname '*phi-3*' -o -iname '*phi3*'` → empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.safetensors' -o -name '*.gguf' -o -name '*.bin' -path '*model*'` → empty. `find / -xdev -name '*.whl'` → empty.\n- `import torch` / `import numpy` → ModuleNotFoundError. `pip list` = 105 packages, all distro tooling; grep for torch|transformers|datasets|accelerate|hugging|numpy|scipy|safetensors|tokenizers|eval|ptq|sklearn → no match.\n- Network: socket to pypi.org:443 → gaierror \"[Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution\"; `pip install numpy` fails; no /etc/pip.conf; ~/.cache absent; /tmp was empty.\n- nproc=224, os.sched_getaffinity=224 (\"0-223\"), no /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max; Intel Xeon Platinum 8570; `free -g`: 2011 total, 1935 available, no swap.\n- `df`: /workspace 1.0T, 1018G used, 6.2G avail (100%); /tmp tmpfs 1006G. 100 MB write probe to /workspace succeeded then removed.\n- /usr/bin has gcc, gcc-15, g++, cc, make, git, git-lfs, curl, wget; no cmake, no nvcc.\n\nARITHMETIC grounding for §2.1/§3/§5/§7 (python3, pure arithmetic on assumed constants — no model, no data, no eval):\n- head_dim = 3072//32 = 96; (96 & 95) != 0 → not a power of two; 96 = 3*32; 3072 = 3*1024; 8192 power-of-two = True.\n- Params ≈ 3.82 B (113.25 M/layer: fused qkv 3072×9216, o_proj, gate_up 3072×16384, down 8192×3072, +embed/lm_head/norms); bf16 = 7.64 GB; int4+scale ≈ 2.15 GB.\n- GPTQ Hessians fp32: qkv 38 MB, gate_up 38 MB, down_proj 268 MB → ~344 MB/layer sequential. Calibration 128×4096 = 524,288 tokens.\n- Assumed task n's and binomial SE at p=.5: piqa 1838/1.17pp, arc_easy 2376/1.03, arc_challenge 1172/1.46, hellaswag 10042/0.50, winogrande 1267/1.40, openbookqa 500/2.24, mmlu 14042/0.42, truthfulqa 817/1.75, gsm8k 1319/1.38; core6 n = 17,195.\n- Prefill cost at 150 tok/prompt (truthfulqa ×104 targets): core6 ≈2.6M tokens, full battery ≈17.6M. At 40 tok/s → core6 17.9 h/cell, full 122.4 h/cell; ×12 cells = 215 h / 1469 h. At 15 tok/s → 573 h / 3917 h.\n- ppl cost parametric: 25k tokens ≈ 6×4096 windows (≈10 min/cell at 40 tok/s); 282,209 tokens ≈ 69 windows (≈118 min/cell).\n- 3 paired repeats: SD .2 → paired-diff SE .163, MDE .462; SD 1.0 → SE .816, MDE 2.311.\n- McNemar vs independent-proportion MDE (Z=2.80, 80% power): n=125 → 7.9pp vs 17.7pp at 10% discordance; n=293 → 5.2 vs 11.6; n=2510 → 1.8 vs 4.0; n=500 → 4.0 vs 8.9. Basis for the §5.3 underpowering claim.\n\nNOT EVIDENCE (model-knowledge, unverified, enumerated as §1 checklist items): all QuaRot code-layout claims (power-of-two assertion site, post-RoPE online Hadamard, find_layers key dicts, models/llama.py copies, RTN path) and all Phi-3 config values. No perplexity, accuracy, or runtime outcome of the proposed experiment exists anywhere in this document. Scratch scripts deleted; /workspace left containing only task.json.", "assumptions": ["DESIGN ONLY: no experiment was executed; no figure in the document is a measured outcome. Throughput, prompt-length and task-size numbers are costing assumptions to be replaced by host measurements.", "Binding resource bound is 2 effective CPU cores per the task statement, despite the sandbox reporting 224 CPUs with no visible cgroup quota; the tier must be re-decided after measuring one cell's tokens/s on the real host.", "Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct weights, C4 calibration data, WikiText-2 and the zero-shot suites are obtainable on a separate host with network access; none exist here.", "Every Phi-3 config value and every QuaRot code-architecture claim is unverified model knowledge gated behind the section-1 checklist; in particular 'online Hadamard applied post-RoPE' determines whether the whole port strategy is valid.", "Weight-only W4/W6/W8 with FP16 activations and KV cache, symmetric weights, groupsize 128, percdamp 0.01, embed_tokens and lm_head excluded from quantization but still rotated; W4A4 out of scope.", "Primary rotations are exactly orthogonal block-diagonal constructions blkdiag(H32 x3) for head_dim 96 and blkdiag(H1024 x3) for hidden 3072; dense Had(96) only if verifiable on the host, with no existence claim made.", "T0 numerical tolerances (0.02 absolute / 0.05 percent relative ppl, zero accuracy change on a 500-example probe) are my proposed thresholds; the brief specifies none.", "Success thresholds (+10 percent relative ppl acceptability; rho >= 0.5 x rho_LLama for 'generalizes well'; interaction I>0) are my proposals; the brief defines no criterion.", "One fixed chat-template formatting policy and one pinned modeling path (native transformers phi3 vs trust_remote_code) apply to every cell including the BF16 reference and T0.", "Execution host runs Python 3.10/3.11 in a conda env; the sandbox's Python 3.14 cannot host the pinned torch/transformers stack.", "The LLaMA-3-8B positive control is optional-to-conclusion; if unfunded, only the intrinsic generalization criterion G-int survives.", "Zero-shot subsamples are drawn once with a fixed seed and shared by every cell so that McNemar pairing remains valid."], "uncertainties": ["Whether QuaRot applies the q/k Hadamards post-RoPE (exactness-preserving) or pre-RoPE offline - the single most consequential unknown; if pre-RoPE, dim-96 becomes a RoPE-compatibility problem and section 2 must be rewritten.", "Whether Phi-3-mini has tied word embeddings; if tied, the residual-stream rotation forces a de-facto untying that T0 bounds numerically but not interpretationally.", "How large the WikiText-2 test split is in Phi-3 tokens, which sets per-cell ppl cost and therefore which tier is affordable.", "The actual repeat-to-repeat SD of GPTQ delta-ppl across calibration subsets; the MDE figures are conditional on an assumed SD and are unknown until the 4-bit repeats run.", "Whether a verifiable Had(96) construction is obtainable; if not, the block-diagonal-mixing confound cannot be separated from a genuine Phi-3 finding within this budget.", "Whether the instruct-calibration arm reverses the RTN/GPTQ ordering obtained under C4; if so the primary headline must be qualified and that arm promoted.", "Real CPU throughput and scaling on the execution host (memory-bandwidth-bound), which decides whether the T1/T2 split or full-battery-for-all-cells is executed.", "Whether the pinned lm-evaluation-harness/transformers versions expose the Phi-3 chat template consistently across all tasks; template drift across cells would confound every zero-shot delta.", "Whether folding rotation into fused qkv_proj/gate_up_proj introduces non-exactness beyond what the module-class bisection in the T0 failure path can localise."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-840895a5717055e1", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-840895a5717055e1", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"answer\": \"# QuaRot \\u2192 Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct: full experiment design (DESIGN ONLY)\\n\\n**Status.** No experiment has been run, none can be run in this sandbox, and no measured, estimated, or simulated outcome appears anywhere in this document. Every environment statement comes from probes executed this session; every architecture/code-layout/task-size statement is an **item to verify** (\\u00a71) or an **assumption** (\\u00a78). All throughput and duration figures are arithmetic under explicitly labelled assumed constants, not measurements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Pre-flight verification checklist (blocking; run before anything else)\\n\\nNothing downstream is meaningful until these are checked against the real `config.json`, the real tree, and the real task definitions. Each is an open item, never a fact.\\n\\n**A. Model config** (`microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct/config.json` + `generation_config.json`):\\n1. `hidden_size`, `intermediate_size`, `num_hidden_layers`, `num_attention_heads`; **`head_dim` derived as `hidden//heads`** \\u2014 confirm 96 and that no explicit `head_dim` field exists.\\n2. `num_key_value_heads` (expected 32 \\u2192 GQA ratio 1, plain MHA). Per your ruling the GQA framing is **removed from the writeup**; this item exists only to confirm we are not silently relying on an untested `repeat_kv` path.\\n3. `vocab_size`, `eos_token_id`/`<|end|>` id, and **`tie_word_embeddings`** (drives \\u00a72.4).\\n4. `rope_scaling` (`longrope`, `short_factor`, `long_factor`, `mscale`), `original_max_position_embeddings`, `max_position_embeddings`, `attention_scaling`, any logit softcap, `rms_norm_eps`, `use_mlp_bias`, `use_sliding_window`/`sliding_window`.\\n5. **Which modeling path is pinned** \\u2014 native `transformers.models.phi3` vs `trust_remote_code=True` custom code. Pick one, record its commit, use it for the BF16 reference, all 12 cells, and the exactness gate. A mismatch here is a silent confound.\\n6. Confirm fused-module layout and widths: `self_attn.qkv_proj` (out 3\\u00b7hidden), `self_attn.o_proj`, `mlp.gate_up_proj` (out 2\\u00b7intermediate), `mlp.down_proj`, and whether any attention/MLP **bias** exists (RMSNorm in `input_layernorm`/`post_attention_layernorm` only?).\\n\\n**B. QuaRot tree** (all claims about it in this design are model-knowledge, unverified):\\n7. Locate the power-of-two assertion \\u2014 expected in the Hadamard utility (`utils/hadamard_matrix.py`, `get_had`/`FastHadamardTransform`) asserting on matrix size \\u2014 and record every call site that passes a head-dim or hidden-dim size.\\n8. Locate where the q/k Hadamards are applied and **confirm they are applied post-RoPE**, so H\\u1d40H cancels exactly in the score and no RoPE-commutation constraint exists. If they are instead applied pre-RoPE offline, \\u00a72.2 changes completely and the port needs a RoPE-compatible construction; this single fact gates the whole Phi-3 story.\\n9. Locate the module-selection dispatch (`llama_attention_keys`, `llama_mlp_keys` in `find_layers`) and the per-model modeling copies (`models/llama.py`, `models/llama_gptq.py`) to scope the `models/phi3.py` port.\\n10. Locate `merge_ln`/`fuse_ln_weight_into_proj` and `rotate_model`; confirm which modules are excluded from quantization by default and how `lm_head`/`embed_tokens` are treated.\\n11. Confirm the RTN path (`--quant_method normal`) rounds the **already-rotated** weights per channel with no calibration, and that GPTQ consumes the same rotated weights \\u2014 i.e. rotation is genuinely upstream of both algorithms, which is what makes the 2\\u00d72\\u00d73 crossing valid.\\n12. Record pinned versions (torch, transformers \\u2014 Phi-3 support landed ~4.41, `lm_eval`) and confirm wheels exist for the host Python. The sandbox's **3.14 will not do**; a 3.10/3.11 env is required.\\n\\n**C. Harness**: per-task split sizes `n`, template/fewshot format, and confirmation that loglikelihood tasks score deterministically.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Port specification: organizing the port around head_dim 96 and hidden 3072\\n\\n### 2.1 Non-power-of-two rotations (your ruling 2)\\nPrimary rotation = **block-diagonal exact Hadamard reusing the existing Walsh\\u2013Hadamard path** \\u2014 exactly orthogonal, and asserting nothing we cannot construct:\\n- head_dim 96 \\u2192 `blkdiag(H\\u2083\\u2082, H\\u2083\\u2082, H\\u2083\\u2082)` (96 = 3\\u00b732);\\n- hidden 3072 \\u2192 `blkdiag(H\\u2081\\u2080\\u2082\\u2084, H\\u2081\\u2080\\u2082\\u2084, H\\u2081\\u2080\\u2082\\u2084)` (3072 = 3\\u00b71024);\\n- intermediate 8192 \\u2192 full `H\\u2088\\u2081\\u2089\\u2082` (clean, 2\\u00b9\\u00b3), so the MLP-side rotation stays exactly as upstream.\\n\\nScaling 1/\\u221ablock. Mixing occurs within a 32- or 1024-block, never across blocks \\u2014 the central compromise (\\u00a79).\\n**Pre-registered sensitivity arm, 4-bit only:** dense `Had(96)` for the head dim, **conditional on a construction we can independently verify on the host** (brute-force check `H H\\u1d40 = 96 I`). No existence claim is made here. If nothing verifiable is available, the arm is dropped and reported as not run.\\n**R\\u2032 arm (seeded random orthogonal, identical placement):** 4-bit, both algorithms. Separates placement/exactness from Hadamard-specific structure: if R\\u2032 \\u2248 QuaRot, any Phi-3 deficit is about placement/geometry rather than Hadamard weakness at dim 96.\\n\\n### 2.2 Attention (head_dim 96)\\nPer-head rotations stay block-diagonal over heads. If item 8 confirms post-RoPE online application, the *block structure* choice cannot break exactness \\u2014 it can only weaken outlier mixing, which is exactly what S-RAND and S-HAD96 measure. v/o_proj take the offline per-head pair (H on the v output side, H\\u1d40 on the o_proj input side).\\n\\n### 2.3 Fused projections\\nLLaMA-shaped code rotates `q_proj/k_proj/v_proj` and `gate_proj/up_proj` independently; Phi-3 exposes `qkv_proj`/`gate_up_proj`. The port must apply head-aligned (q|k|v) and (gate|up) slices of the block-diagonal rotation to the fused weight, or un-fuse into views before rotation and re-fuse after. Harmless for GPTQ (per-module Hessian, groups along the input dim); fatal for rotation folding if done naively. **Verification probe:** after rotation, before any quantization, the fused and un-fused implementations must agree to fp64 tolerance.\\n\\n### 2.4 Residual stream, tying, lm_head\\n`embed_tokens`/`lm_head` are **excluded from quantization** (your ruling 4) but must still be **rotated** \\u2014 the residual stream lives in the rotated basis, so G is folded into the embedding output and G\\u1d40 into `lm_head`. \\\"Unquantized\\\" \\u2260 \\\"unrotated\\\"; this is the most likely site of a silent T0 failure. If `tie_word_embeddings` is true, rotation forces a **de-facto untying** (rotated embeddings, lm_head carrying G\\u1d40); the exactness gate is what proves this was done correctly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Cell matrix, with the inference each cell buys\\n\\nCommon to all cells: Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct; weight-only W\\u2208{4,6,8} symmetric; FP16 activations and FP16 KV cache (`a_bits=v_bits=k_bits=0`); **W4A4 explicitly out of scope**; `embed_tokens`/`lm_head` unquantized; identical calibration, modeling path, `OMP_NUM_THREADS` and batch size (numerical-drift control); groupsize g=128, `percdamp`=0.01.\\n\\n### 3.1 PRIMARY reported result \\u2014 the literal 2\\u00d73 (your ruling 1)\\n| Cell | Rotation | Algo | Bits |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Q-R4 / Q-R6 / Q-R8 | QuaRot (blkdiag-H) | RTN | 4 / 6 / 8 |\\n| Q-G4 / Q-G6 / Q-G8 | QuaRot (blkdiag-H) | GPTQ | 4 / 6 / 8 |\\n\\nReported as the direct answer to the stated question and, explicitly, **as a descriptive table: no rotation main effect and no rotation\\u00d7algorithm interaction is estimable from it.**\\n\\n### 3.2 REQUIRED controls \\u2014 completing the 2\\u00d72\\u00d73\\n| Cell | Rotation | Algo | Bits | Inference bought |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| N-R4 / N-R6 / N-R8 | Identity | RTN | 4 / 6 / 8 | Rotation effect within RTN at each bit; whether unrotated RTN is already competitive at 6/8-bit |\\n| N-G4 / N-G6 / N-G8 | Identity | GPTQ | 4 / 6 / 8 | Rotation effect within GPTQ; makes R\\u00d7A identifiable, i.e. whether rotation and GPTQ rounding are redundant or complementary |\\n\\n**B1** BF16 reference (ppl + full battery) \\u2014 the anchor for every \\u0394.\\n**T0** Q-Gate16 \\u2014 QuaRot rotation, 16-bit, no quantization (\\u00a76).\\n\\u00a75 reports the 2\\u00d73 and the 2\\u00d72\\u00d73 analyses **separately, never blended.**\\n\\n### 3.3 Sensitivity / diagnostic arms\\n| Arm | Cells | Why |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **S-INST** | 4-bit \\u00d7 {RTN, GPTQ} with an **instruct-style** calibration set (fixed small instruction slice) | GPTQ is calibration-distribution-sensitive, RTN largely is not; the C4-vs-instruct mismatch could **manufacture** an RTN/GPTQ ranking. **Survives budget cuts; PTB does not** (your ruling 5). If it reverses the C4 ordering, the primary headline is downgraded to \\\"under C4 calibration\\\". |\\n| S-GROUP | 4-bit: RTN at g=128 and g=\\u22121; GPTQ at g=\\u22121 | Separates the rounding-algorithm effect from the group-wise-representation effect. |\\n| S-DAMP | GPTQ W4, percdamp {0.01, 0.1, 1.0} | Prevents reading an ill-conditioned-Hessian artifact as an algorithmic effect. |\\n| S-HAD96 | dense Had(96), W4, both algos | **Conditional** on a verifiable construction only. |\\n| S-RAND | R\\u2032 random orthogonal, W4, both algos | Placement/exactness vs Hadamard structure. |\\n| D-DIAG | per-channel activation max/median ratio, kurtosis, top-1%-energy **pre vs post rotation** per layer class; per-layer \\u2016\\u0174X\\u2212WX\\u2016_F; Hessian condition number | Mechanism: does rotation actually isotropize Phi-3 activations the way it does LLaMA's? Cheap and CPU-friendly. |\\n| **T3-CTRL** | **Optional:** LLaMA-3-8B (or Llama-2-7B) 4-bit QuaRot-RTN/GPTQ + Identity-RTN | The only thing that makes \\\"generalizes\\\" a comparative claim, and the only way to separate a port bug from a genuine Phi-3 finding. **Optional-to-conclusion, budget-dependent, clearly marked** (your ruling 3). |\\n| Dropped | PTB perplexity | First cut (your ruling 5). |\\n\\nTotals: 12 factorial + B1 + T0 + 2 (S-INST) + 3 (S-GROUP) + 2 (S-DAMP) + 2 (S-RAND) + 0\\u20132 (S-HAD96) + 0\\u20134 (T3-CTRL).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Evaluation protocol\\n\\n**Perplexity.** WikiText-2 test split, **4096-token non-overlapping windows, no stride**, plus the **2048-token slice** for comparability with published QuaRot/GPTQ tables. Tokenizer and template identical across cells. The exact test token count is a verification item, not a fact \\u2014 it sets the per-cell cost. Primary quantities are **\\u0394ppl = ppl(cell) \\u2212 ppl(BF16)** and **\\u0394ppl_rel = \\u0394ppl / ppl(BF16)**; raw ppl secondary; both context lengths always reported.\\n\\n**Zero-shot.** `lm-evaluation-harness`, `--model hf`, one pinned task-YAML/template family, identical `--num_fewshot` across cells. **core6**: piqa, arc_easy, arc_challenge, hellaswag, winogrande, openbookqa (0-shot, loglikelihood). **Extended**: mmlu (5-shot), truthfulqa_mc, gsm8k (8-shot CoT, greedy/temp-0 \\u2014 deliberately brittle; 4-bit cells only). Record **per-example correctness**, not just means \\u2014 that is what makes \\u00a75.3 pairing possible.\\n\\n**Instruct-model formatting (consequential, fixed once).** One chat-template policy for the entire grid (recommend the Phi-3 chat template with the harness's documented fewshot-as-single-message option; store the rendered prompt verbatim in the artifacts). Applied identically to BF16, rotated and unrotated cells, so it can shift all cells together but cannot create a contrast.\\n\\n**Tiering (your ruling 7).** **T1** = ppl at both contexts + fixed-seed **25% paired subsample of core6** \\u2014 mandatory for **all 12 cells**. **T2** = full battery, full splits \\u2014 4-bit cells (Q-R4, Q-G4, N-R4, N-G4) + B1 (+ S-INST cells, which are 4-bit by construction). **T3** = optional LLaMA control, S-HAD96, PTB.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Seeds, repeats, variance, statistics\\n\\n### 5.1 Where variance enters\\n1. **Calibration subset** \\u2014 the dominant real source for GPTQ: **3 disjoint C4 subsets, 128\\u00d74096 = 524,288 tokens each**, seeds 101/102/103. Repeats are **paired by subset across all cells**, so every cell-to-cell comparison is within-subset.\\n2. **Rotation draw** \\u2014 zero for block-diagonal Hadamard (deterministic, no seed); seeds 201/202/203 apply only to R\\u2032.\\n3. **Numerical nondeterminism** \\u2014 bf16/fp32 accumulation order varies with thread count and batch size and can exceed the effect sizes of interest. Fix `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, batch size, dtype and kernel set identically for **all cells including BF16 and T0**; run the BF16 reference twice at different thread counts as a drift probe. If that drift exceeds the smallest \\u0394 in the grid, report \\u0394 against an explicit numerical floor rather than claiming effects beneath it.\\n4. **Eval sampling** \\u2014 none (loglikelihood, greedy generation); the only stochasticity is the fixed-seed 25% T1 subsample, drawn once and shared by every cell.\\n5. RTN itself is deterministic given the rotated weights.\\n\\n**Repeats.** 4-bit: 3 repeats (variance and the ranking question both live here). 6/8-bit: 1 repeat, flagged as **descriptive only, with no variance estimate by design**.\\n\\n### 5.2 Pre-registered headline 1 \\u2014 mechanism (your ruling 6)\\nTwo-factor rotation \\u00d7 algorithm on \\u0394ppl_rel, analysed **separately at 4 and 6 bits**, calibration subset as blocking factor:\\n\\n**I = [\\u0394ppl_rel(N-R) \\u2212 \\u0394ppl_rel(N-G)] \\u2212 [\\u0394ppl_rel(Q-R) \\u2212 \\u0394ppl_rel(Q-G)]** at each bit.\\n\\nDirectional hypothesis **I > 0**: GPTQ's advantage over RTN shrinks once rotation removes outliers, i.e. the mechanisms are partially redundant. Estimated on differences paired by calibration subset, with 95% CIs from (i) subset-level resampling over the 3 repeats and (ii) a window-level bootstrap over WikiText-2 eval windows. Conditional on an assumed repeat SD, the paired-difference MDE with 3 repeats is \\u22480.46 ppl at SD 0.2 and \\u22482.3 ppl at SD 1.0 (arithmetic; the true SD is unknown until run). **Disconfirming:** CI excluding 0 on the negative side \\u2192 mechanisms complementary, contradicting the redundancy reading; CI covering 0 \\u2192 interaction **not identified**, and we claim nothing either way and report the null.\\n\\n### 5.3 Pre-registered headline 2 \\u2014 generalization (your ruling 6)\\n**G-int (intrinsic, always available).** QuaRot transfers to Phi-3 iff at 4-bit: (i) \\u0394ppl_rel(Q-X) < \\u0394ppl_rel(N-X) with CI excluding 0 for **both** X \\u2208 {RTN, GPTQ}; (ii) \\u0394ppl_rel monotone in bits (W4 > W6 > W8) in all four rotation\\u00d7algo combinations; (iii) rotation does not *hurt* at 8-bit (\\u0394ppl_rel(Q-X) \\u2264 \\u0394ppl_rel(N-X) + numerical floor). Proposed practical acceptability (mine, since the brief is silent): QuaRot-GPTQ W4 within **+10% relative** of BF16 WikiText-2 ppl.\\n\\n**G-cmp (comparative, needs T3).** Relative benefit \\u03c1_X = \\u0394ppl_rel^Phi3(N-X) / \\u0394ppl_rel^Phi3(Q-X), and \\u03c1_X^LLaMA at matched bits. **\\\"Generalizes well\\\" iff \\u03c1_X^Phi3 \\u2265 0.5\\u00b7\\u03c1_X^LLaMA for at least one algorithm and \\u03c1_X^Phi3 > 1 for both.** Between 0 and 0.5\\u00b7: partial. **Disconfirming:** \\u03c1_X^Phi3 \\u2264 1 for both algorithms at 4-bit (rotation buys nothing on Phi-3), or \\u03c1 < 0.25\\u00b7\\u03c1^LLaMA (effect collapses), which we would attribute to the block-diagonal mixing compromise (\\u00a79), using S-RAND/S-HAD96 as discriminators.\\n\\n**Zero-shot inference.** All contrasts are **paired McNemar** on per-example correctness between cells sharing example IDs \\u2014 never independent-proportion tests, especially not on 25% subsamples \\u2014 with Holm\\u2013Bonferroni over the pre-registered contrast family. Always report task `n`, accuracy, and binomial SE. Power note (arithmetic at an assumed 10% discordance rate): at the full openbookqa split (n\\u2248500) McNemar detects \\u22484.0 pp, but on its 25% subsample (n\\u2248125) only \\u22487.9 pp, whereas hellaswag's subsample (n\\u22482510) still detects \\u22481.8 pp. **Consequence:** openbookqa, arc_challenge and winogrande subsamples are underpowered for cell-vs-cell zero-shot contrasts **by construction** and are reported as descriptive only; zero-shot claims rest on ppl, the pooled core6 mean, and the T2 full-split cells.\\n\\n**Sensitivity reporting rule.** If S-INST reverses the RTN/GPTQ ordering obtained under C4, the primary result is qualified \\\"under C4 calibration\\\" and the calibration arm is promoted into the main table.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. T0 exactness gate and failure path (your ruling 8)\\n\\n**Gate.** Q-Gate16 (rotation, 16-bit, no quantization) must reproduce the BF16 reference within stated tolerance **before any grid cell is interpreted**: **|\\u0394ppl| \\u2264 0.02 absolute and \\u2264 0.05% relative** on WikiText-2 at both 4096 and 2048 windows, plus **exactly zero** per-task accuracy differences on a fixed 500-example probe. A rotation is a change of basis, so any consistent accuracy change indicates a real modeling difference, not noise.\\n\\n**If it fails we stop and debug; we do not report grid cells.** Diagnostic order, most likely first: (1) G folded into `embed_tokens` / G\\u1d40 into `lm_head`, and the tie handling of \\u00a72.4; (2) fused `qkv_proj`/`gate_up_proj` head-aligned slicing (\\u00a72.3); (3) `merge_ln` consumer set without double-folding; (4) per-head block layout vs RoPE split-half pairing (\\u00a72.2); (5) RoPE/longrope/mscale/attention-scaling differences between BF16 and the ported file; (6) dtype of the rotation application (fp32 vs bf16). Bisection: run the gate with `merge_ln` disabled, then module-class by module-class (attention-only, then MLP-only), localising the failing transformation before touching a quantizer. A failed gate makes all 12 cells uninterpretable, not merely uncertain \\u2014 the gate failure *is* the finding in that branch.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Feasibility, resources, tiering (your ruling 10)\\n\\n**Measured in this sandbox this session:** `/workspace` contains one 499-byte `task.json`, not a git repo; no torch/numpy/transformers/datasets/eval code; no weights, no HF cache, no datasets, no wheelhouse; DNS fails and `pip install` fails; Python 3.14.4; 224 CPUs visible with affinity `0-223` and no visible cgroup quota; 2011 GB RAM (~1935 available); `/workspace` 1.0 TB at 100% with **6.2 GB free**; `/tmp` tmpfs ~1006 GB; gcc/make/curl present but useless offline. **Nothing in this design can execute here.**\\n\\n**Planning bound.** The **2-effective-core limit is adopted as the binding planning assumption** because that is what the task environment states; it is *not* what the sandbox reports (224), and the discrepancy is unresolved.\\n\\n**Arithmetic under stated assumptions** (assumed, not measured: 3.8 B params, 7.64 GB bf16 weights, ~7.6 GFLOP/token, a throughput band of 15\\u2013100 tok/s on 2 cores):\\n- GPTQ Hessian scratch \\u2248 **344 MB per layer** (2\\u00d73072\\u00b2 + 8192\\u00b2 fp32, layer-sequential) \\u2014 RAM is never the constraint; 8192\\u00b2 Cholesky solves are seconds, forward passes dominate.\\n- Calibration: 524,288 tokens per subset \\u00d7 3 subsets \\u00d7 GPTQ cells.\\n- WikiText-2 ppl cost scales with the (unverified) test token count: ~25 k tokens \\u2248 6 windows; ~282 k \\u2248 69 windows \\u2192 10\\u2013120 min per cell at 40 tok/s. Cheap.\\n- **Zero-shot is the binding constraint.** core6 \\u2248 2.6 M prompt-tokens (assumed 150 tok/prompt), full battery \\u2248 17.6 M (truthfulqa dominates via ~104 targets/question). At 40 tok/s: core6 \\u2248 **18 h per cell**, full battery \\u2248 **122 h per cell** \\u2192 12 cells \\u2248 **215 h** and **1469 h** respectively (at 15 tok/s: 573 h / 3917 h). This is precisely why T1 uses paired 25% subsamples and the full battery is restricted to 4-bit + references, and why S-INST/S-GROUP/S-DAMP/S-RAND survive (4-bit-only, cheap) while PTB and T3 are what get cut.\\n- **Sensitivity to core count:** if the host really exposes 224 cores, CPU GEMM scaling is memory-bandwidth-bound (realistically ~10\\u201340\\u00d7 aggregate, not 112\\u00d7) and cells parallelise embarrassibly. At ~20\\u00d7 aggregate with 12 cells in parallel, T1 becomes near-free and the **full battery for all 12 cells** comes into reach; the T1/T2 split would then be replaced by \\\"T2 for everything, T3 included,\\\" and the \\u00a75.3 subsampling caveat disappears. Decision rule: measure one cell's tok/s before committing, then choose the tier, and record the measured throughput in the artifact so the tier choice is auditable.\\n- **Disk:** `/tmp` tmpfs for bf16 weights (~7.6 GB) and quantized dumps (~2.15 GB per 4-bit cell); `/workspace` (6.2 GB free) for metrics JSON and per-example predictions only. Never write model artifacts to `/workspace`.\\n\\n**Reporting contract.** (a) primary 2\\u00d73 table with \\u0394ppl / \\u0394ppl_rel / \\u0394acc and raw values; (b) the 2\\u00d72\\u00d73 table with rotation main effects and the interaction, reported separately; (c) arms table; (d) T0 gate result and measured throughput; (e) an explicit \\\"design only, not executed\\\" banner on every table.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Assumptions vs sources\\n\\n| # | Statement | Status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | /workspace holds only task.json; no torch/numpy/transformers; no weights/datasets; offline; 224 CPUs, 2 TB RAM, 6.2 GB free on /workspace | **Measured this session** |\\n| 2 | 2 cores effectively usable | **Task-stated; contradicted by sandbox affinity; adopted as planning bound** |\\n| 3 | Phi-3 config (3072 / 8192 / 32\\u00d732 / head_dim 96 / kv_heads 32 / vocab 32064 / longrope / tie) | **Model-knowledge, unverified \\u2192 \\u00a71.A** |\\n| 4 | QuaRot layout: power-of-two assert, post-RoPE online H, `find_layers` keys, fused-module mismatch, `models/llama.py` copies, RTN = `--quant_method normal` | **Model-knowledge, unverified \\u2192 \\u00a71.B** |\\n| 5 | Weight-only W4/W6/W8, FP16 acts+KV, embed/lm_head unquantized, W4A4 out of scope | **Your ruling 4** |\\n| 6 | blkdiag H32\\u00d73 / H1024\\u00d73 primary; Had(96) 4-bit conditional; R\\u2032 4-bit | **Your ruling 2** |\\n| 7 | 2\\u00d73 primary, Identity-rotation RTN/GPTQ required as controls, reported separately | **Your ruling 1** |\\n| 8 | Phi-3 the only subject; LLaMA-3-8B 4-bit as optional T3 positive control | **Your ruling 3** |\\n| 9 | C4 128\\u00d74096 primary; instruct-style 4-bit arm required; PTB optional, first cut | **Your ruling 5** |\\n| 10 | Interaction at 4/6-bit and matched-bit relative degradation as the two headlines | **Your ruling 6; the numeric thresholds are my proposal** |\\n| 11 | WikiText-2 primary, 4096+2048 windows, lm-eval-harness battery, T1/T2 tiering, McNemar | **Your ruling 7; task list, shot counts and the exact T1/T2 line are mine within your constraint** |\\n| 12 | T0 tolerances (0.02 abs / 0.05% rel / zero accuracy diff) | **My proposal \\u2014 brief silent** |\\n| 13 | groupsize 128, percdamp 0.01, symmetric weights, seeds 101-103/201-203 | **My proposal \\u2014 brief silent** |\\n| 14 | +10% relative acceptability; \\u03c1 \\u2265 0.5\\u00b7\\u03c1^LLaMA for \\\"generalizes well\\\" | **My proposal \\u2014 brief gives no success criterion** |\\n| 15 | One chat-template policy | **My proposal \\u2014 brief silent** |\\n| 16 | 15\\u2013100 tok/s, 150 tok/prompt, task n's, WikiText-2 token count | **Costing assumptions; measure on host, then fix the tier** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Limitations\\n\\n1. **Design only.** Nothing was run and this sandbox cannot run it (no torch, no numpy, no weights, no datasets, no network). Every quantity here is a plan, a tolerance, or arithmetic on assumed constants.\\n2. **The block-diagonal mixing compromise is the central internal threat.** Because head_dim 96 and hidden 3072 are not powers of two, \\\"QuaRot on Phi-3\\\" here means `blkdiag(H\\u2083\\u2082\\u00d73)` and `blkdiag(H\\u2081\\u2080\\u2082\\u2084\\u00d73)`, which mix less thoroughly than a full Hadamard and may leave outliers partly intact. A negative Phi-3 result therefore cannot by itself distinguish \\\"QuaRot does not generalize to Phi-3\\\" from \\\"block-diagonal rotation is too weak at dim 96\\\". S-RAND and (only if a verifiable Had(96) exists) S-HAD96 are the discriminators, and S-HAD96 is conditional \\u2014 this limitation may not be resolvable within budget.\\n3. **Calibration confound** for the RTN/GPTQ ranking; S-INST exists precisely because a C4-vs-instruct mismatch could produce an artifact rather than a property of the algorithms.\\n4. **Zero-shot subsampling underpower** affects several core tasks by construction (\\u00a75.3); zero-shot contrasts at 6/8-bit are descriptive only.\\n5. **6/8-bit cells are single-repeated** \\u2014 absence of variance there is by design, not evidence of stability.\\n6. **Unverified substrate.** Both the Phi-3 config and every QuaRot code claim are model-knowledge; \\u00a71 is blocking because a wrong assumption there (especially items 8 and 9) invalidates the port and the headline.\\n7. **Single model, single shape.** One Phi-3 variant, no GQA stress (ratio 1) and no MoE; conclusions concern Phi-3-mini's dense-MHA shape, not \\\"non-LLaMA models\\\" generally. If T3 is unfunded, the comparative half of the generalization claim (G-cmp) is lost and only G-int survives.\\n8. **Tied-embedding de-tying** (if item 3 confirms tying) makes the rotated model structurally different from the released checkpoint even at 16-bit in the parameter-tie sense; T0 bound